2026-08-01 16:40:03 [deepseek-v4-flash]    That’s fine for a standard WOZ2 TRKS chunk (1280 bytes), but it will read past a smaller chunk
2026-08-01 16:40:03 [deepseek-v4-flash] if the file is malformed. Consider passing `chunkSize` and limiting the loop to `Math.min(160,
2026-08-01 16:40:03 [deepseek-v4-flash] chunkSize / 8)`.
2026-08-01 16:40:03 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 16:40:03 [deepseek-v4-flash] 3. Bounds check in `decodeDos33Sector()` is slightly off.
2026-08-01 16:40:03 [deepseek-v4-flash]    You read 342 nibbles from `dataStart`, so the check should be:
2026-08-01 16:40:03 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 16:40:03 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 16:40:03 [deepseek-v4-flash]    if (dataStart + 342 > nibbles.length) return null;
2026-08-01 16:40:03 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 16:40:03 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 16:40:04 [deepseek-v4-flash]    The current `dataStart + 343 >= nibbles.length` rejects a valid sector that ends exactly after
2026-08-01 16:40:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] the 342 data nibbles (though real disks usually have an epilogue after them, so it may never matter
2026-08-01 16:40:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] in practice).
2026-08-01 16:40:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 16:40:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] 4. `loadNib()` is still a stub.
2026-08-01 16:40:04 [deepseek-v4-flash]    It currently just logs a failure message; `.nib` loading won’t do anything yet.
2026-08-01 16:40:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 16:40:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] 5. If the WOZ2 file still says “no nibbles”:
2026-08-01 16:40:04 [deepseek-v4-flash]    - Log `tmap[17 * 4]` — if it’s `0xFF`, that quarter‑track isn’t mapped.
2026-08-01 16:40:04 [deepseek-v4-flash]    - Log the first 10 nibbles produced by `bitstreamToNibbles()`.
2026-08-01 16:40:04 [deepseek-v4-flash]    - Check whether the 4‑and‑4 address decode order (`odd`/`even`) matches the track/sector order
2026-08-01 16:40:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] in that particular WOZ. If only one file fails, the encoding order or TMAP mapping is the usual
2026-08-01 16:40:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] suspect.
2026-08-01 16:40:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 16:40:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] Happy to help debug one of the failing WOZ files next, or add the remaining official 6502 opcodes
2026-08-01 16:40:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] to `machine.ts`.
