2026-08-01 17:46:39 [deepseek-v4-flash] Looking at the code, the sector detection works (16 per track), but the decoder has a few issues to
2026-08-01 17:46:39 [deepseek-v4-flash] fix before it can produce usable disk images:
2026-08-01 17:46:40 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 17:46:40 [deepseek-v4-flash] 1. `decodeDos33Sector()` uses undefined `track` and `sector`
2026-08-01 17:46:40 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 17:46:40 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 17:46:40 [deepseek-v4-flash] if (foundTrack !== track || foundSector !== sector) { ... }
2026-08-01 17:46:40 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 17:46:40 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 17:46:40 [deepseek-v4-flash] `track` and `sector` are not parameters. Either pass them in:
2026-08-01 17:46:40 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 17:46:40 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 17:46:40 [deepseek-v4-flash] function decodeDos33Sector(nibbles: number[], expectedTrack: number, expectedSector: number): DecodedSector[] | null
2026-08-01 17:46:40 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 17:46:40 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 17:46:40 [deepseek-v4-flash] or remove the check entirely — the address field in the nibbles already contains the actual
2026-08-01 17:46:40 [deepseek-v4-flash] track/sector.
2026-08-01 17:46:40 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 17:46:40 [deepseek-v4-flash] 2. Address field offsets are off by 2
2026-08-01 17:46:40 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 17:46:40 [deepseek-v4-flash] Standard DOS 3.3 address field:
2026-08-01 17:46:40 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 17:46:40 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 17:46:40 [deepseek-v4-flash] D5 AA 96
2026-08-01 17:46:40 [deepseek-v4-flash] track odd/even   (i+3, i+4)
2026-08-01 17:46:40 [deepseek-v4-flash] sector odd/even  (i+5, i+6)
2026-08-01 17:46:40 [deepseek-v4-flash] checksum odd/even (i+7, i+8)
2026-08-01 17:46:40 [deepseek-v4-flash] DE AA EB
2026-08-01 17:46:40 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 17:46:40 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
