2026-08-01 18:19:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] The decode logic is close, but there are a few issues that will prevent you from building a usable
2026-08-01 18:19:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] disk image.
2026-08-01 18:19:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 18:19:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] 1. Address field offsets are wrong
2026-08-01 18:19:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 18:19:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] In a standard DOS 3.3 address field:
2026-08-01 18:19:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 18:19:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 18:19:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] D5 AA 96
2026-08-01 18:19:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] volume odd/even    (i+3, i+4)
2026-08-01 18:19:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] track odd/even     (i+5, i+6)
2026-08-01 18:19:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] sector odd/even    (i+7, i+8)
2026-08-01 18:19:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] checksum odd/even  (i+9, i+10)
2026-08-01 18:19:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] DE AA EB
2026-08-01 18:19:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 18:19:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 18:19:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] Your current code reads:
2026-08-01 18:19:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 18:19:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 18:19:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] track  = decodeAddressByte(bytes[(i+3)%n], bytes[(i+4)%n]);
2026-08-01 18:19:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] sector = decodeAddressByte(bytes[(i+5)%n], bytes[(i+6)%n]);
2026-08-01 18:19:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] crc    = decodeAddressByte(bytes[(i+7)%n], bytes[(i+8)%n]);
2026-08-01 18:19:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 18:19:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 18:19:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] That makes `track` = volume (usually $FE), `sector` = actual track, and `crc` = actual sector. Fix
2026-08-01 18:19:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] it:
2026-08-01 18:19:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 18:19:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 18:19:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] track  = decodeAddressByte(bytes[(i+5)%n], bytes[(i+6)%n]);
2026-08-01 18:19:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] sector = decodeAddressByte(bytes[(i+7)%n], bytes[(i+8)%n]);
2026-08-01 18:19:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] crc    = decodeAddressByte(bytes[(i+9)%n], bytes[(i+10)%n]);
2026-08-01 18:19:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 18:19:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 18:19:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] You can optionally verify the checksum: it should equal `volume ^ track ^ sector`.
2026-08-01 18:19:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 18:19:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] 2. Sector count is now 32, not 16
2026-08-01 18:19:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 18:19:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] You push `i` for address prologues and `-i` for data prologues, so `sectors.length` counts both. If
2026-08-01 18:19:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] you want to verify 16 sectors per track, either count only positive entries:
2026-08-01 18:19:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 18:19:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 18:19:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] const addressCount = sectors.filter(v => v >= 0).length;
2026-08-01 18:19:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] console.log({ n: track.bytes.length, count: addressCount });
2026-08-01 18:19:04 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] or return a structured object.
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 3. Decoded blocks are discarded
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] `blocks` is local to `detectSectors` and never returned or associated with the track/sector. To
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] build a disk in memory, you need to match each address prologue to the following data
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] prologue, then store the decoded 256 bytes in a `disk[track][sector]` array.
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] Here’s a more complete approach:
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] interface DecodedSector {
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 	track: number;
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 	sector: number;
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 	offset: number;
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 	bytes: Uint8Array;
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] }
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] function decodeTrack(rawTrack: Uint8Array): DecodedSector[] {
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 	const n = rawTrack.length;
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 	const result: DecodedSector[] = [];
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 	for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 		// Address prologue
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 		if (rawTrack[i] === 0xD5 && rawTrack[(i+1)%n] === 0xAA && rawTrack[(i+2)%n] === 0x96) {
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 			const track = decodeAddressByte(rawTrack[(i+5)%n], rawTrack[(i+6)%n]);
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 			const sector = decodeAddressByte(rawTrack[(i+7)%n], rawTrack[(i+8)%n]);
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 			// Search for the data prologue after this address field
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 			for (let j = i + 9; j < i + 600; j++) {
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 				const k = j % n;
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 				if (rawTrack[k] === 0xD5 && rawTrack[(k+1)%n] === 0xAA && rawTrack[(k+2)%n] === 0xAD) {
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 					const dataStart = (k + 3) % n;
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 					// Read 342 nibbles with wraparound
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 					const nibbles = new Uint8Array(342);
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 					for (let p = 0; p < 342; p++) {
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 						nibbles[p] = rawTrack[(dataStart + p) % n];
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 					}
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 					const bytes = decodeDos33Sector(nibbles);
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 					if (bytes) {
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 						result.push({ track, sector, offset: k, bytes });
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 					}
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 					break;
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 				}
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 			}
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 		}
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 	}
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 	return result;
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] }
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] Then you can build a full disk:
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] const disk: Uint8Array[][] = Array.from({ length: 35 }, () => new Array(16));
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] for (let t = 0; t < tracks.length; t++) {
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 	const decoded = decodeTrack(tracks[t].bytes);
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 	for (const d of decoded) {
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 		if (d.track >= 0 && d.track < 35 && d.sector >= 0 && d.sector < 16) {
2026-08-01 18:19:05 [deepseek-v4-flash] 			disk[d.track][d.sector] = d.bytes;
2026-08-01 18:19:06 [deepseek-v4-flash] 		}
2026-08-01 18:19:06 [deepseek-v4-flash] 	}
2026-08-01 18:19:06 [deepseek-v4-flash] }
2026-08-01 18:19:06 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 18:19:06 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 18:19:06 [deepseek-v4-flash] 4. Minor issues
2026-08-01 18:19:06 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 18:19:06 [deepseek-v4-flash] - `async function loadNib(...): Array<Track>` should be `Promise<Array<Track>>`.
2026-08-01 18:19:06 [deepseek-v4-flash] - `decodeDos33Sector` uses a shared global `temp`. Make it local to avoid stale data on errors.
2026-08-01 18:19:06 [deepseek-v4-flash] - The unused `Nibbles` interface and `testBraille` import can be removed.
2026-08-01 18:19:06 [deepseek-v4-flash] - `payload` as a global is unnecessary; declare it inside `loadNib` and return tracks.
2026-08-01 18:19:06 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 18:19:06 [deepseek-v4-flash] Once the address offsets are fixed, you should see proper track/sector values in the logs, and
2026-08-01 18:19:06 [deepseek-v4-flash] you’ll be one step away from mounting the decoded disk in your Disk II emulation.
