2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] The address-field decoding is now correct — all 16 sectors per track are being found, and the CRC
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] values are consistent with `volume ^ track ^ sector`. For example, track 0 sector 2 gives `42 ^ 2 =
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] 40`, exactly matching the log.
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] A few observations from the output:
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] - The physical sector order varies per track (e.g. track 0 starts at sector 2, track 1 at sector 0,
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] track 2 at sector 10). That's normal — DOS 3.3 uses different skew/interleave patterns per track,
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] so don't try to impose a fixed order. Just store each sector by its decoded number.
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] - Track 34 doesn't appear in the logs. It may be unformatted, intentionally empty, or using
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] non-standard markers. Worth checking separately if the game needs it.
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] - The decoded data blocks are still not linked to their track/sector numbers. Next step is to match
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] each address prologue with the following data prologue, then store `disk[track][sector]`.
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] Example pairing logic:
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] interface DecodedSector {
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] 	track: number;
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] 	sector: number;
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] 	bytes: Uint8Array;
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] }
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] function decodeTrack(raw: Uint8Array): DecodedSector[] {
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] 	const n = raw.length;
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] 	const out: DecodedSector[] = [];
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] 	for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] 		if (raw[i] === 0xD5 && raw[(i+1)%n] === 0xAA && raw[(i+2)%n] === 0x96) {
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] 			const track    = decodeAddressByte(raw[(i+5)%n], raw[(i+6)%n]);
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] 			const sector   = decodeAddressByte(raw[(i+7)%n], raw[(i+8)%n]);
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] 			// find the data prologue that follows this address field
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] 			for (let j = i + 11; j < i + 600; j++) {
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] 				const k = j % n;
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] 				if (raw[k] === 0xD5 && raw[(k+1)%n] === 0xAA && raw[(k+2)%n] === 0xAD) {
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] 					const start = (k + 3) % n;
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] 					const nibbles = new Uint8Array(342);
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] 					for (let p = 0; p < 342; p++) {
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] 						nibbles[p] = raw[(start + p) % n];
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] 					}
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] 					out.push({ track, sector, bytes: decodeDos33Sector(nibbles) });
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] 					break;
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] 				}
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] 			}
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] 		}
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] 	}
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] 	return out;
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] }
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 19:02:36 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 19:02:37 [deepseek-v4-flash] Then build the whole disk:
2026-08-01 19:02:37 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 19:02:37 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 19:02:37 [deepseek-v4-flash] const disk: Uint8Array[][] = Array.from({ length: 35 }, () => new Array(16));
2026-08-01 19:02:37 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-01 19:02:37 [deepseek-v4-flash] for (let t = 0; t < tracks.length; t++) {
2026-08-01 19:02:37 [deepseek-v4-flash] 	for (const s of decodeTrack(tracks[t].bytes)) {
