2026-08-03 09:42:11 [deepseek-v4-flash] To set a background highlight (like a highlighter effect) and then clear it, you can use
2026-08-03 09:42:11 [deepseek-v4-flash] these ANSI codes:
2026-08-03 09:42:11 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-03 09:42:11 [deepseek-v4-flash] - Set background color: `\x1b[<color>m` where `<color>` is:
2026-08-03 09:42:11 [deepseek-v4-flash]   - 40–47 (standard) or 100–107 (bright)
2026-08-03 09:42:11 [deepseek-v4-flash]   - Example: `\x1b[43m` = yellow background
2026-08-03 09:42:11 [deepseek-v4-flash] - Reverse video (inverts foreground/background, also a highlight effect): `\x1b[7m`
2026-08-03 09:42:11 [deepseek-v4-flash] - Clear background only: `\x1b[49m` (sets default background)
2026-08-03 09:42:11 [deepseek-v4-flash] - Turn off reverse video: `\x1b[27m`
2026-08-03 09:42:11 [deepseek-v4-flash] - Reset everything (background, bold, etc.): `\x1b[0m`
2026-08-03 09:42:11 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
