2026-08-03 13:37:35 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Store cursor position (row/column)
2026-08-03 13:37:35 [claude-haiku-4-5] - During `displayC64()` render, check if current char position matches cursor
2026-08-03 13:37:35 [claude-haiku-4-5] - If `frameCount & 32` (or similar blink rate), substitute/invert that character
2026-08-03 13:37:35 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-03 13:37:35 [claude-haiku-4-5] The cursor isn't an overlay; it's a character replacement in the displayed text, just like typing
2026-08-03 13:37:35 [claude-haiku-4-5] normally overwrites screen RAM.
2026-08-03 13:37:35 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
