2026-08-04 18:41:43 [claude-haiku-4-5] That's fine for storing MIDI input pointers by ID. A few observations:
2026-08-04 18:41:43 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-04 18:41:43 [claude-haiku-4-5] 1. Type safety: If you're working with actual MIDI input objects rather than raw pointers,
2026-08-04 18:41:43 [claude-haiku-4-5] consider whether `Deno.UnsafePointer` is the right type. You might want a more specific interface.
2026-08-04 18:41:43 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-04 18:41:43 [claude-haiku-4-5] 2. Initialization: The empty object is reasonable if you're populating it dynamically.
2026-08-04 18:41:43 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
