2026-08-04 18:41:59 [claude-haiku-4-5] The `Set` method on a `Map` is used to add or update a key-value pair:
2026-08-04 18:41:59 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-04 18:41:59 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-04 18:41:59 [claude-haiku-4-5] const midiInputs = new Map<number, Deno.UnsafePointer>();
2026-08-04 18:41:59 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-04 18:41:59 [claude-haiku-4-5] // Add or update
2026-08-04 18:41:59 [claude-haiku-4-5] midiInputs.set(1, pointerValue);
2026-08-04 18:41:59 [claude-haiku-4-5] midiInputs.set(2, anotherPointer);
2026-08-04 18:41:59 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-04 18:41:59 [claude-haiku-4-5] // Update existing
2026-08-04 18:41:59 [claude-haiku-4-5] midiInputs.set(1, newPointerValue);
2026-08-04 18:41:59 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-04 18:41:59 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-04 18:41:59 [claude-haiku-4-5] With your `Record` approach, you'd use direct assignment instead:
2026-08-04 18:41:59 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-04 18:41:59 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-04 18:41:59 [claude-haiku-4-5] midiInputs[1] = pointerValue;
2026-08-04 18:41:59 [claude-haiku-4-5] midiInputs[2] = anotherPointer;
2026-08-04 18:41:59 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-04 18:41:59 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-04 18:41:59 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Map advantages:*
2026-08-04 18:41:59 [claude-haiku-4-5] - `has(key)` - check if key exists
2026-08-04 18:41:59 [claude-haiku-4-5] - `get(key)` - retrieve value (returns `undefined` if missing)
2026-08-04 18:41:59 [claude-haiku-4-5] - `delete(key)` - remove entry
2026-08-04 18:41:59 [claude-haiku-4-5] - `clear()` - remove all entries
2026-08-04 18:41:59 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Better iteration with `.forEach()`, `.entries()`, `.keys()`, `.values()`
2026-08-04 18:41:59 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-04 18:41:59 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Record advantages:*
2026-08-04 18:41:59 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Simpler syntax for basic use cases
2026-08-04 18:41:59 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Slightly faster for small datasets
2026-08-04 18:41:59 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-04 18:41:59 [claude-haiku-4-5] For MIDI device management, I'd lean toward `Map` since you'll likely need those convenience
2026-08-04 18:41:59 [claude-haiku-4-5] methods.
