2026-08-05 09:15:10 [claude-haiku-4-5] Critical Issues
2026-08-05 09:15:10 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-05 09:15:10 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Drop share persistence* (notes.md item 5)
2026-08-05 09:15:10 [claude-haiku-4-5] The `/drop` command reports success but doesn't persist—shares reappear after `/share` is called.
2026-08-05 09:15:10 [claude-haiku-4-5] This suggests the UI updates locally while `roha.sharedFiles` retains the old state. The drop
2026-08-05 09:15:10 [claude-haiku-4-5] handler should synchronize state before returning.
2026-08-05 09:15:10 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-05 09:15:10 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Help file resolution* (notes.md item 2)
2026-08-05 09:15:10 [claude-haiku-4-5] `forge.md` lookup fails on startup. The error occurs when `/help` runs before the working directory
2026-08-05 09:15:10 [claude-haiku-4-5] stabilizes. Consider resolving the help path relative to the relay executable location rather than
2026-08-05 09:15:10 [claude-haiku-4-5] `cwd()`.
2026-08-05 09:15:10 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-05 09:15:10 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Glob expansion in /share* (notes.md item 1)
2026-08-05 09:15:10 [claude-haiku-4-5] `/share *.md` isn't implemented. The `shareCommand()` function in relay.ts currently accepts a
2026-08-05 09:15:10 [claude-haiku-4-5] single path. To support globs:
2026-08-05 09:15:10 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Use `expandGlob()` from deno/fs
2026-08-05 09:15:10 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Collect results into a batch before calling `addShare()` for each match
2026-08-05 09:15:10 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Sort results to ensure predictable ordering on large trees
2026-08-05 09:15:10 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-05 09:15:10 [claude-haiku-4-5] Design Observations
2026-08-05 09:15:10 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-05 09:15:10 [claude-haiku-4-5] • History metadata loss during squash*
2026-08-05 09:15:10 [claude-haiku-4-5] When `squashMessages()` merges consecutive same-role messages, it discards `price`, `elapsed`, and
2026-08-05 09:15:10 [claude-haiku-4-5] `tool_calls`. If you're tracking cost per model or reasoning depth, that data vanishes. Consider
2026-08-05 09:15:10 [claude-haiku-4-5] preserving these in a metadata field or skipping squash entirely for analysis passes.
2026-08-05 09:15:10 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-05 09:15:10 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Tool result inconsistency*
2026-08-05 09:15:10 [claude-haiku-4-5] The four history formatters (`plainHistory`, `strictHistory`, `multiHistory`, etc.) handle
2026-08-05 09:15:10 [claude-haiku-4-5] `role:"tool"` differently. The `[TEST3]` echo in multiHistory suggests incomplete refactoring. A
2026-08-05 09:15:10 [claude-haiku-4-5] pluggable history interface would make this testable and extensible.
2026-08-05 09:15:10 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-05 09:15:10 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Project reset without confirmation*
2026-08-05 09:15:10 [claude-haiku-4-5] Item 4 notes that `/reset` should prompt before clearing all projects. Silently flushing
2026-08-05 09:15:10 [claude-haiku-4-5] `roha.sharedFiles` and history risks accidental loss. Add a `confirm()` step before clearing.
