2026-08-05 09:15:52 [claude-haiku-4-5] The biblispec project is a well-curated reference for Unicode, typography, and linguistic systems.
2026-08-05 09:15:52 [claude-haiku-4-5] Several observations:
2026-08-05 09:15:52 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-05 09:15:52 [claude-haiku-4-5] Strong Design
2026-08-05 09:15:52 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-05 09:15:52 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Structural clarity* — The JSON organization (books/, biblispec.json as payload) is sound.
2026-08-05 09:15:52 [claude-haiku-4-5] Separating concerns like machine specs, audio circuits, and phrases into modular JSON files keeps
2026-08-05 09:15:53 [claude-haiku-4-5] the payload navigable.
2026-08-05 09:15:53 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-05 09:15:53 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Unicode scholarship* — The Egyptian Hieroglyphic coverage (1072 codepoints across
2026-08-05 09:15:53 [claude-haiku-4-5] U+1300–U+1342) is thorough. The categorical breakdown (Women, Eyes, Fish, Birds, Animals) makes the
2026-08-05 09:15:53 [claude-haiku-4-5] block approachable. Similar care shown in Alchemical symbols, Ogham, Cherokee, Vai, and CJK
2026-08-05 09:15:53 [claude-haiku-4-5] Enclosed Digits.
2026-08-05 09:15:53 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-05 09:15:53 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Linguistic breadth* — Hebrew, Coptic, Greek, Latin, Reo Māori, Linear B—each with
2026-08-05 09:15:53 [claude-haiku-4-5] alphabet data (lower, upper, uncommon variants). Practical for text processing pipelines.
2026-08-05 09:15:53 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-05 09:15:53 [claude-haiku-4-5] Content Observations
2026-08-05 09:15:53 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-05 09:15:53 [claude-haiku-4-5] • "Labyrinthine typography" in scratch.md* — The discussion of Escher-style interlocking
2026-08-05 09:15:53 [claude-haiku-4-5] graffiti (tessellation, Penrose illusion, mechanical wildstyle) is creative but feels orphaned.
2026-08-05 09:15:53 [claude-haiku-4-5] This reads like research notes. Consider either:
2026-08-05 09:15:53 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Expanding it into a proper spec subsection (e.g., `books/typography.json` with glyph tessellation
2026-08-05 09:15:53 [claude-haiku-4-5] rules)
2026-08-05 09:15:53 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Removing it if it's exploratory scaffolding
2026-08-05 09:15:53 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-05 09:15:53 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Array vs. Class skirmish* — You note the conflict in machinespec.json (ordered arrays
2026-08-05 09:15:53 [claude-haiku-4-5] like `software-architecture: [...]` vs. keyed objects like `video-game: {Speed Race: {...}}`). This
2026-08-05 09:15:53 [claude-haiku-4-5] is genuine design tension:
2026-08-05 09:15:53 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Arrays preserve insertion order and support iteration
2026-08-05 09:15:53 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Objects allow semantic keys and O(1) lookup
2026-08-05 09:15:53 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Mixed use forces consumers to check type at runtime
2026-08-05 09:15:53 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-05 09:15:53 [claude-haiku-4-5] Consider standardizing: either all keyed objects with a `_order` metadata array, or all arrays with
2026-08-05 09:15:53 [claude-haiku-4-5] a `key` property on each item.
2026-08-05 09:15:53 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-05 09:15:53 [claude-haiku-4-5] • pheme word building* — The prefix/suffix system (pre62, suff27) is linguistically sound
