2026-08-05 17:33:23 [claude-haiku-4-5] TED RAM Banking
2026-08-05 17:33:23 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-05 17:33:23 [claude-haiku-4-5] Yes, exactly. The TED (Plus/4) has ROM/RAM overlay at C000-FFFF. When RAM is banked in,
2026-08-05 17:33:23 [claude-haiku-4-5] writes should go to RAM even if ROM normally occupies that space.
2026-08-05 17:33:23 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-05 17:33:23 [claude-haiku-4-5] Current Code Issue
2026-08-05 17:33:23 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-05 17:33:23 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-05 17:33:23 [claude-haiku-4-5] writeTED(address: number, value: number) {
2026-08-05 17:33:23 [claude-haiku-4-5] 	const mem = this.memory;
2026-08-05 17:33:23 [claude-haiku-4-5] 	// ...
2026-08-05 17:33:23 [claude-haiku-4-5] 	mem[address] = value;  // ← Always writes to unified memory array
2026-08-05 17:33:23 [claude-haiku-4-5] }
2026-08-05 17:33:23 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-05 17:33:23 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-05 17:33:23 [claude-haiku-4-5] This works if your memory model keeps both ROM and RAM in the same `Uint8Array`. But if
2026-08-05 17:33:23 [claude-haiku-4-5] you're reading ROM on reads and need to write RAM on writes, you need explicit routing.
2026-08-05 17:33:23 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-05 17:33:23 [claude-haiku-4-5] Solution
2026-08-05 17:33:23 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-05 17:33:23 [claude-haiku-4-5] Track the RAM bank state and route accordingly:
2026-08-05 17:33:23 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-05 17:33:23 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-05 17:33:23 [claude-haiku-4-5] ramBanked = false;  // Already declared in your code
2026-08-05 17:33:23 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-05 17:33:23 [claude-haiku-4-5] writeTED(address: number, value: number) {
2026-08-05 17:33:23 [claude-haiku-4-5] 	const mem = this.memory;
2026-08-05 17:33:23 [claude-haiku-4-5] 	const label = this.addresLabel(address);
2026-08-05 17:33:23 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-05 17:33:23 [claude-haiku-4-5] 	switch(address) {
2026-08-05 17:33:23 [claude-haiku-4-5] 		case 0xFF3E:  // enable rom
2026-08-05 17:33:23 [claude-haiku-4-5] 			this.ramBanked = false;
2026-08-05 17:33:23 [claude-haiku-4-5] 			break;
2026-08-05 17:33:23 [claude-haiku-4-5] 		case 0xFF3F:  // enable ram
