2026-08-06 11:32:00 [claude-haiku-4-5] No, they're different keyboard matrices.
2026-08-06 11:32:00 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-06 11:32:00 [claude-haiku-4-5] • VIC-20* uses a 8x8 matrix (64 keys max)
2026-08-06 11:32:00 [claude-haiku-4-5] • C64* uses a 8x8 matrix but with different key assignments and layout
2026-08-06 11:32:00 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-06 11:32:00 [claude-haiku-4-5] The electrical scanning method is similar (rows/columns), but the physical keyboard layout differs
2026-08-06 11:32:01 [claude-haiku-4-5] and the ROM character maps are different. If you're writing keyboard scanning code, you'll need
2026-08-06 11:32:01 [claude-haiku-4-5] separate lookup tables for each machine.
2026-08-06 11:32:01 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-06 11:32:01 [claude-haiku-4-5] What are you working on - emulation, hardware interfacing, or something else?
