2026-08-07 09:32:29 [claude-haiku-4-5] "ADC":{"opcodes":"69 65 75 6D 7D 79 61 71","flags":"NZCV","label":"ADD MEMORY TO ACCUMULATOR WITH CARRY","spec":15}
2026-08-07 09:32:29 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-07 09:32:29 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-07 09:32:29 [claude-haiku-4-5] • Spec 15* has 8 opcodes for 8 addressing modes. The `profile` array confirms this:
2026-08-07 09:32:29 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-07 09:32:29 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-07 09:32:29 [claude-haiku-4-5] {"bytes":[2,2,2,3,3,3,2,2],"cycles":[2,3,4,4,4,4,6,5]}
2026-08-07 09:32:30 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-07 09:32:30 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-07 09:32:30 [claude-haiku-4-5] That's the spec index mapping to:
2026-08-07 09:32:30 [claude-haiku-4-5] 1. `69` - Immediate (#$xx) → 2 bytes
2026-08-07 09:32:30 [claude-haiku-4-5] 2. `65` - Zeropage ($xx) → 2 bytes
2026-08-07 09:32:30 [claude-haiku-4-5] 3. `75` - Zeropage,X ($xx,X) → 2 bytes
2026-08-07 09:32:30 [claude-haiku-4-5] 4. `6D` - Absolute ($xxxx) → 3 bytes
2026-08-07 09:32:30 [claude-haiku-4-5] 5. `7D` - Absolute,X ($xxxx,X) → 3 bytes
2026-08-07 09:32:30 [claude-haiku-4-5] 6. `79` - Absolute,Y ($xxxx,Y) → 3 bytes
2026-08-07 09:32:30 [claude-haiku-4-5] 7. `61` - (Indirect,X) ($xx,X) → 2 bytes
2026-08-07 09:32:30 [claude-haiku-4-5] 8. `71` - (Indirect),Y ($xx),Y → 2 bytes
2026-08-07 09:32:30 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-07 09:32:30 [claude-haiku-4-5] The Fix
2026-08-07 09:32:30 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-07 09:32:30 [claude-haiku-4-5] Instead of a monolithic switch on `mode`, `parse6502` needs to:
2026-08-07 09:32:30 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-07 09:32:30 [claude-haiku-4-5] 1. Map the detected `addressMode` to its index (0-7)
2026-08-07 09:32:30 [claude-haiku-4-5] 2. Look up the correct opcode from `instruction.opcodes` using that index
2026-08-07 09:32:30 [claude-haiku-4-5] 3. Encode the operand bytes based on the mode and profile
2026-08-07 09:32:30 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-07 09:32:30 [claude-haiku-4-5] The `spec` value is the key—it tells you which profile to use and implicitly which addressing modes
2026-08-07 09:32:30 [claude-haiku-4-5] are valid for that instruction.
2026-08-07 09:32:30 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
