2026-08-07 09:33:43 [claude-haiku-4-5] Looking at your notes.txt error:
2026-08-07 09:33:43 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-07 09:33:43 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-07 09:33:43 [claude-haiku-4-5] opcode: "AND",
2026-08-07 09:33:43 [claude-haiku-4-5] spec: 15,
2026-08-07 09:33:43 [claude-haiku-4-5] codes: "29 25 35 2D 3D 39 21 31",
2026-08-07 09:33:43 [claude-haiku-4-5] code: { mode: 1, ref8: 16 }
2026-08-07 09:33:43 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-07 09:33:43 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-07 09:33:43 [claude-haiku-4-5] Mode 1 is `Zeropage` with `ref8: 16`.
2026-08-07 09:33:43 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-07 09:33:43 [claude-haiku-4-5] For spec 15, the opcodes array maps to addressing modes in order:
2026-08-07 09:33:43 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Index 0: `29` - Immediate
2026-08-07 09:33:43 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Index 1: `25` - Zeropage ← Your case
2026-08-07 09:33:43 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Index 2: `35` - Zeropage,X
2026-08-07 09:33:43 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Index 3: `2D` - Absolute
2026-08-07 09:33:43 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Index 4: `3D` - Absolute,X
2026-08-07 09:33:43 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Index 5: `39` - Absolute,Y
2026-08-07 09:33:43 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Index 6: `21` - (Indirect,X)
2026-08-07 09:33:43 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Index 7: `31` - (Indirect),Y
2026-08-07 09:33:43 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-07 09:33:43 [claude-haiku-4-5] So for `AND $10`:
2026-08-07 09:33:43 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Opcode: `25`
2026-08-07 09:33:43 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Operand: `10` (the ref8 value)
2026-08-07 09:33:44 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Result: `25 10`
2026-08-07 09:33:44 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-07 09:33:44 [claude-haiku-4-5] The `code.mode` (1) directly indexes into the opcodes string. Split it and grab index 1, then
2026-08-07 09:33:44 [claude-haiku-4-5] append the operand bytes per the profile.
2026-08-07 09:33:44 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
