2026-08-07 09:35:46 [claude-haiku-4-5] Mode Detection Function
2026-08-07 09:35:46 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-07 09:35:46 [claude-haiku-4-5] Here's a structured approach to detect all addressing modes from operand syntax:
2026-08-07 09:35:46 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-07 09:35:46 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-07 09:35:46 [claude-haiku-4-5] function detectMode(operand: string): Mode {
2026-08-07 09:35:46 [claude-haiku-4-5] 	const op = operand.toUpperCase();
2026-08-07 09:35:46 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-07 09:35:46 [claude-haiku-4-5] 	// Immediate: #$xx or #%xxxxxxxx or #'c'
2026-08-07 09:35:46 [claude-haiku-4-5] 	if (op.startsWith("#")) return Mode.Immediate;
2026-08-07 09:35:46 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-07 09:35:46 [claude-haiku-4-5] 	// Indirect indexed: ($xx,X)
2026-08-07 09:35:46 [claude-haiku-4-5] 	if (op.startsWith("(") && op.endsWith(",X)")) return Mode.Indirect8;
2026-08-07 09:35:46 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-07 09:35:46 [claude-haiku-4-5] 	// Indirect: ($xxxx) or ($xx)
2026-08-07 09:35:46 [claude-haiku-4-5] 	if (op.startsWith("(") && op.endsWith(")")) return Mode.Indirect16;
2026-08-07 09:35:46 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-07 09:35:46 [claude-haiku-4-5] 	// Indexed indirect: ($xx),Y
2026-08-07 09:35:46 [claude-haiku-4-5] 	if (op.startsWith("(") && op.endsWith("),Y")) return Mode.IndirectY;
2026-08-07 09:35:46 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-07 09:35:46 [claude-haiku-4-5] 	// Absolute,X: $xxxx,X (4 hex digits)
2026-08-07 09:35:46 [claude-haiku-4-5] 	if (op.includes(",X")) {
2026-08-07 09:35:46 [claude-haiku-4-5] 		const addr = op.replace(",X", "");
2026-08-07 09:35:46 [claude-haiku-4-5] 		if (addr.startsWith("$") && addr.length === 5) return Mode.AbsoluteX;
2026-08-07 09:35:46 [claude-haiku-4-5] 		if (addr.startsWith("$") && addr.length === 3) return Mode.ZeroPageX;
2026-08-07 09:35:46 [claude-haiku-4-5] 	}
2026-08-07 09:35:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-07 09:35:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] 	// Absolute,Y: $xxxx,Y
2026-08-07 09:35:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] 	if (op.includes(",Y")) {
2026-08-07 09:35:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] 		const addr = op.replace(",Y", "");
2026-08-07 09:35:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] 		if (addr.startsWith("$") && addr.length === 5) return Mode.AbsoluteY;
2026-08-07 09:35:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] 		if (addr.startsWith("$") && addr.length === 3) return Mode.ZeroPageY;
2026-08-07 09:35:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] 	}
2026-08-07 09:35:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-07 09:35:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] 	// Absolute or Zeropage: $xxxx or $xx
2026-08-07 09:35:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] 	if (op.startsWith("$")) {
2026-08-07 09:35:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] 		if (op.length === 5) return Mode.Absolute;
2026-08-07 09:35:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] 		if (op.length === 3) return Mode.Zeropage;
2026-08-07 09:35:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] 	}
2026-08-07 09:35:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-07 09:35:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] 	// Branch: label reference
2026-08-07 09:35:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] 	if (op.length > 0 && !op.startsWith("$") && !op.startsWith("#") && !op.startsWith("(")) {
2026-08-07 09:35:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] 		return Mode.Branch;
2026-08-07 09:35:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] 	}
2026-08-07 09:35:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-07 09:35:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] 	// Implied/None
2026-08-07 09:35:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] 	return Mode.None;
2026-08-07 09:35:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] }
2026-08-07 09:35:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-07 09:35:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2026-08-07 09:35:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] This replaces your `addressMode` function and returns a clean Mode enum. Then `parse6502` can use
2026-08-07 09:35:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] the mode directly to index into the opcodes string.
2026-08-07 09:35:47 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
