2026-08-07 10:07:34 [claude-haiku-4-5] - spec 5: 2 bytes, 2 cycles → Branch (BCC, BEQ, etc.)
2026-08-07 10:07:34 [claude-haiku-4-5] - spec 6: 3 bytes, 6 cycles → JSR (absolute)
2026-08-07 10:07:34 [claude-haiku-4-5] - spec 7: 2-3 bytes → BIT instruction variants
2026-08-07 10:07:34 [claude-haiku-4-5] - spec 8: 3 bytes, 3-5 cycles → JMP (absolute or indirect)
2026-08-07 10:07:35 [claude-haiku-4-5] - spec 9: 2-3 bytes → CPX/CPY (immediate, zeropage, absolute)
2026-08-07 10:07:35 [claude-haiku-4-5] - spec 10: 2-3 bytes → STX/STY
2026-08-07 10:07:35 [claude-haiku-4-5] - spec 11: 2-3 bytes, 5-7 cycles → DEC (zeropage variants to absolute)
2026-08-07 10:07:35 [claude-haiku-4-5] - spec 12: 1-3 bytes → ASL, LSR, ROL, ROR (accumulator + addressing modes)
2026-08-07 10:07:35 [claude-haiku-4-5] - spec 13: 2-3 bytes → LDX/LDY variants
2026-08-07 10:07:35 [claude-haiku-4-5] - spec 14: 2-3 bytes → STA (zeropage to indirect,Y)
2026-08-07 10:07:35 [claude-haiku-4-5] - spec 15: 2-3 bytes → ADC, AND, CMP, EOR, LDA, ORA, SBC (most flexible: immediate through
2026-08-07 10:07:35 [claude-haiku-4-5] indirect,Y)
