2026-08-10 07:17:20 [claude-sonnet-5] That's a solid base. A few subtle additions that would round it out without overpowering the
2026-08-10 07:17:20 [claude-sonnet-5] content — since these blocks already carry a lot of visual weight from the Unicode content itself:
2026-08-10 07:17:20 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-08-10 07:17:20 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-08-10 07:17:20 [claude-sonnet-5] #code{
2026-08-10 07:17:20 [claude-sonnet-5] 	margin: 12px;
2026-08-10 07:17:20 [claude-sonnet-5] 	font-size: x-large;
2026-08-10 07:17:20 [claude-sonnet-5] 	padding: 12px;
2026-08-10 07:17:20 [claude-sonnet-5] 	background-color: #f6f6f6;
2026-08-10 07:17:20 [claude-sonnet-5] 	border-left: 3px solid #ccc;
2026-08-10 07:17:20 [claude-sonnet-5] 	border-radius: 4px;
2026-08-10 07:17:20 [claude-sonnet-5] 	line-height: 1.4;
2026-08-10 07:17:20 [claude-sonnet-5] 	overflow-x: auto;
2026-08-10 07:17:20 [claude-sonnet-5] }
2026-08-10 07:17:20 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-08-10 07:17:20 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-08-10 07:17:20 [claude-sonnet-5] A few notes on the choices:
2026-08-10 07:17:20 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-08-10 07:17:20 [claude-sonnet-5] - `padding` — right now `margin` gives space outside the block, but there's nothing pushing
2026-08-10 07:17:20 [claude-sonnet-5] the text away from its own edges, so it can feel cramped against a background or border.
2026-08-10 07:17:20 [claude-sonnet-5] - `background-color` — a very light grey lifts it off the page as a distinct "block"
2026-08-10 07:17:20 [claude-sonnet-5] without shouting. If the rest of the page is on a dark theme, this would need inverting (something
2026-08-10 07:17:20 [claude-sonnet-5] like `#1e1e1e` background with lighter text).
2026-08-10 07:17:20 [claude-sonnet-5] - `border-left` — a thin accent border is a common "this is code/data" visual cue, subtler
2026-08-10 07:17:20 [claude-sonnet-5] than a full border box.
2026-08-10 07:17:20 [claude-sonnet-5] - `line-height` — `<pre>` content defaults to fairly tight line spacing; a touch more
2026-08-10 07:17:20 [claude-sonnet-5] breathing room helps readability at `x-large` size, especially with dense Unicode rows.
2026-08-10 07:17:20 [claude-sonnet-5] - `overflow-x: auto` — given some of your fullwidth/CJK/emoji rows can get quite long, this
2026-08-10 07:17:20 [claude-sonnet-5] prevents the block from blowing out page width and instead gives a horizontal scrollbar only when
2026-08-10 07:17:20 [claude-sonnet-5] needed.
2026-08-10 07:17:20 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-08-10 07:17:20 [claude-sonnet-5] Do you have a colour palette or dark/light theme already established elsewhere in `bibli.css`?
2026-08-10 07:17:20 [claude-sonnet-5] That'll steer whether the background/border colours here should be greyscale-neutral or pull from
2026-08-10 07:17:20 [claude-sonnet-5] an existing accent colour.
