2026-08-11 09:09:21 [gemini-3.6-flash] relocates Screen RAM to `1000`.
2026-08-11 09:09:21 [gemini-3.6-flash] • Current Behavior:
2026-08-11 09:09:21 [gemini-3.6-flash]   * `loadPRG` places program bytes into memory at the address defined by the file's two-byte origin
2026-08-11 09:09:21 [gemini-3.6-flash] header, but does not adjust BASIC pointer zero-page registers (`2B`–`2E`, `37`–`38`).
2026-08-11 09:09:21 [gemini-3.6-flash]   * If the emulator defaults to an expanded RAM map or fixed Screen RAM offsets, unexpanded PRG
2026-08-11 09:09:21 [gemini-3.6-flash] files like Gridrunner will fail to execute or will display corrupted video output due to mismatched
2026-08-11 09:09:21 [gemini-3.6-flash] screen and color memory addresses (`1E00`/`09600` vs `1000`/`09400`).
2026-08-11 09:09:21 [gemini-3.6-flash] 
2026-08-11 09:09:21 [gemini-3.6-flash] 3. VIC-20 Blink Speed
2026-08-11 09:09:22 [gemini-3.6-flash] • Root Cause: Flash/blink timing currently shares the global `frameCount` index derived
2026-08-11 09:09:22 [gemini-3.6-flash] from total CPU cycles divided by `62.5ms` ticks (`sixtieth`).
2026-08-11 09:09:22 [gemini-3.6-flash] • Current Behavior:
2026-08-11 09:09:22 [gemini-3.6-flash]   * In `displayAppleWide`, character blinking uses `frameCount & 64`, whereas Commodore video
2026-08-11 09:09:22 [gemini-3.6-flash] rendering passes through `displayPetScreenWide` on alternate frames (`frameCount & 1`).
2026-08-11 09:09:22 [gemini-3.6-flash]   * Because cycle counting and frame update intervals vary across platform configurations, the
2026-08-11 09:09:22 [gemini-3.6-flash] effective flash rate on the VIC-20 screen output runs faster than intended relative to Apple II
2026-08-11 09:09:22 [gemini-3.6-flash] character attribute toggling.
2026-08-11 09:09:22 [gemini-3.6-flash] 
2026-08-13 07:39:31 [gemini-3.6-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.1 gemini-3.6-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.100 155.1KB 16.68s
2026-08-13 07:39:31 [gemini-3.6-flash] The provided code and log trace present two key components: a disassembly snippet from a Commodore
2026-08-13 07:39:31 [gemini-3.6-flash] PET 2001 ROM initialization sequence and a Deno/TypeScript 6502 emulator implementation
2026-08-13 07:39:31 [gemini-3.6-flash] (`machine.ts`).
2026-08-13 07:39:31 [gemini-3.6-flash] 
2026-08-13 07:39:31 [gemini-3.6-flash] 1. Analysis of the PET 2001 Startup Disassembly
2026-08-13 07:39:31 [gemini-3.6-flash] 
2026-08-13 07:39:31 [gemini-3.6-flash] The disassembly sequence illustrates early hardware detection and state initialization on the MOS
2026-08-13 07:39:31 [gemini-3.6-flash] 6502 processor and 6520/6522 peripheral ICs:
2026-08-13 07:39:31 [gemini-3.6-flash] 
2026-08-13 07:39:31 [gemini-3.6-flash] • PIA1 Configuration (E810–E813):
2026-08-13 07:39:31 [gemini-3.6-flash]   * Reads `PIA1_PB` (`$E812`) and checks flags.
2026-08-13 07:39:31 [gemini-3.6-flash]   * Reads `PIA1_PA` (`E810`), masks high nibbles (`AND #F0`), and writes back `$00` to
2026-08-13 07:39:31 [gemini-3.6-flash] configure/clear line states.
2026-08-13 07:39:31 [gemini-3.6-flash]   * Writes `35` to `PIA1_CRB` (`E813`) to configure Control Register B (setting up CB2 control line
2026-08-13 07:39:31 [gemini-3.6-flash] behavior, typically managing the cassette motor or audio write line).
2026-08-13 07:39:31 [gemini-3.6-flash] • VIA Configuration ($E840):
2026-08-13 07:39:31 [gemini-3.6-flash]   * Reads `VIA_ORB` (`E840`), clears bit 4 (`AND #EF`), and writes back to disable or reset
2026-08-13 07:39:31 [gemini-3.6-flash] specific control signals.
2026-08-13 07:39:31 [gemini-3.6-flash] • Cassette & Timing Handshake Loop (E6F9–E75B):
2026-08-13 07:39:31 [gemini-3.6-flash]   * Polls `PIA1_PB` (`$E812`) to detect signal transitions.
2026-08-13 07:39:31 [gemini-3.6-flash]   * Shifts bit 0 (`LSR A` / `BCS`) to check line state before indexing into system timing tables
2026-08-13 07:39:31 [gemini-3.6-flash] located in ROM at `$E75B,X`.
2026-08-13 07:39:31 [gemini-3.6-flash] 
2026-08-13 07:39:32 [gemini-3.6-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-08-13 07:39:32 [gemini-3.6-flash] 
2026-08-13 07:39:32 [gemini-3.6-flash] 2. Implementation Insights in `machine.ts`
2026-08-13 07:39:32 [gemini-3.6-flash] 
2026-08-13 07:39:32 [gemini-3.6-flash] The emulator architecture cleanly models several retro hardware targets (PET, VIC-20, C64, Plus/4,
2026-08-13 07:39:32 [gemini-3.6-flash] Apple II, and Atari DVG systems). Key observation areas regarding PET and 6502 behavior include:
2026-08-13 07:39:32 [gemini-3.6-flash] 
2026-08-13 07:39:32 [gemini-3.6-flash] • PIA1 Interrupt Line Clearing:
2026-08-13 07:39:32 [gemini-3.6-flash]   * In `readPET()`, reading `E812` explicitly masks bits 6 and 7 off in `E813` (`mem[0xE813] &=
2026-08-13 07:39:32 [gemini-3.6-flash] 0x3f;`). This accurately reflects the hardware behavior of the 6520 PIA where reading Peripheral
2026-08-13 07:39:32 [gemini-3.6-flash] Register B clears active interrupt flags.
2026-08-13 07:39:32 [gemini-3.6-flash] • PETSCII and Display Matrix Mapping:
2026-08-13 07:39:32 [gemini-3.6-flash]   * Video memory is targeted at `$8000` (40×25 matrix). `displayPetScreenWide` maps memory bytes to
2026-08-13 07:39:32 [gemini-3.6-flash] double-width Unicode full-width characters (`petsciiUppercaseWide`), maintaining correct screen
2026-08-13 07:39:32 [gemini-3.6-flash] proportions in terminal environments.
2026-08-13 07:39:32 [gemini-3.6-flash] • Cassette Pulse Integration:
2026-08-13 07:39:32 [gemini-3.6-flash]   * `CassetteRecorder` measures transition deltas in CPU clock cycles (1.023\text MHz). The
2026-08-13 07:39:32 [gemini-3.6-flash] tristate level parser handles signal transitions, matching the timing expectations of PET ROM tape
2026-08-13 07:39:32 [gemini-3.6-flash] reading routines.
2026-08-13 07:39:32 [gemini-3.6-flash] 
2026-08-13 07:39:32 [gemini-3.6-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-08-13 07:39:32 [gemini-3.6-flash] 
2026-08-13 07:39:32 [gemini-3.6-flash] 3. Key Points of Comparison & Considerations
2026-08-13 07:39:32 [gemini-3.6-flash] 
2026-08-13 07:39:32 [gemini-3.6-flash] 1. CB1 / CB2 Interrupt Signal Generation:
2026-08-13 07:39:32 [gemini-3.6-flash]    * In the disassembly trace at `E813`, bit 7 is expected to be toggled during frame cycles or
2026-08-13 07:39:32 [gemini-3.6-flash] cassette pulses. In `tick()`, bit 7 is set directly during vertical blanking (`mem[0xe813] |=
2026-08-13 07:39:32 [gemini-3.6-flash] 0x80;`), satisfying the polling routine at `F77F`–`$F782`.
2026-08-13 07:39:32 [gemini-3.6-flash] 2. Cycle Penalty Handling:
2026-08-13 07:39:32 [gemini-3.6-flash]    * Addressing routines like `readAbsoluteX`, `readAbsoluteY`, and `readIndirectY` account for the
2026-08-13 07:39:32 [gemini-3.6-flash] extra cycle incurred when crossing page boundaries (`(address ^ target) & 0xff00`).
2026-08-13 07:39:32 [gemini-3.6-flash] 3. 6502 Page Boundary JMP Indirect Anomaly:
2026-08-13 07:39:32 [gemini-3.6-flash]    * The `JMP ($xxFF)` implementation explicitly models the hardware bug on the MOS 6502, wrapping
2026-08-13 07:39:32 [gemini-3.6-flash] the high byte fetch within the same page (`(pointer & 0xFF00) | ((pointer + 1) & 0x00FF)`).
2026-08-13 07:39:32 [gemini-3.6-flash] 
