2026-08-13 07:53:10 [gemini-3.6-flash] 2. Assembly Syntax & Accumulator Naming Note
2026-08-13 07:53:10 [gemini-3.6-flash] 
2026-08-13 07:53:10 [gemini-3.6-flash] In standard Motorola 6800 assembly conventions, instructions that operate on Dual Accumulators (A
2026-08-13 07:53:10 [gemini-3.6-flash] and B) are often split into explicit `A` and `B` mnemonics.
2026-08-13 07:53:10 [gemini-3.6-flash] 
2026-08-13 07:53:10 [gemini-3.6-flash] Depending on how your assembler/emulator parses mnemonics, you may want to decide whether to keep
2026-08-13 07:53:10 [gemini-3.6-flash] root mnemonics or expand them:
