2026-08-13 07:55:29 [gemini-3.6-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.1 gemini-3.6-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.117 181.3KB 9.45s
2026-08-13 07:55:29 [gemini-3.6-flash] Yes, the logical progression (from simplest/no-operand modes to operand-based and calculated modes)
2026-08-13 07:55:29 [gemini-3.6-flash] is appropriate. However, there is a redundancy in the terminology for the M6800.
2026-08-13 07:55:29 [gemini-3.6-flash] 
2026-08-13 07:55:29 [gemini-3.6-flash] Key Observation: "Direct" vs. "Zero Page"
2026-08-13 07:55:29 [gemini-3.6-flash] 
2026-08-13 07:55:29 [gemini-3.6-flash] In Motorola terminology, "Direct" mode is 8-bit addressing (0000–00FF). MOS
2026-08-13 07:55:29 [gemini-3.6-flash] Technology later renamed this concept to "Zero Page" for the 6502.
2026-08-13 07:55:29 [gemini-3.6-flash] 
2026-08-13 07:55:29 [gemini-3.6-flash] For a Motorola 6800 specification, having both `"Direct"` and `"Zero Page"` is duplicate, as they
2026-08-13 07:55:29 [gemini-3.6-flash] refer to the exact same hardware addressing mechanism.
2026-08-13 07:55:29 [gemini-3.6-flash] 
2026-08-13 07:55:29 [gemini-3.6-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-08-13 07:55:29 [gemini-3.6-flash] 
2026-08-13 07:55:29 [gemini-3.6-flash] Recommended Clean Order (6 Modes)
2026-08-13 07:55:29 [gemini-3.6-flash] 
2026-08-13 07:55:29 [gemini-3.6-flash] Removing `"Zero Page"` leaves you with the standard 6 addressing modes defined in official Motorola
2026-08-13 07:55:29 [gemini-3.6-flash] 6800 documentation, ordered logically by operand size and calculation complexity:
2026-08-13 07:55:29 [gemini-3.6-flash] 
2026-08-13 07:55:29 [gemini-3.6-flash] 
2026-08-13 07:55:29 [gemini-3.6-flash] "addressmode": [
2026-08-13 07:55:29 [gemini-3.6-flash] 	"Inherent",
2026-08-13 07:55:29 [gemini-3.6-flash] 	"Immediate",
2026-08-13 07:55:29 [gemini-3.6-flash] 	"Direct",
2026-08-13 07:55:29 [gemini-3.6-flash] 	"Extended",
2026-08-13 07:55:29 [gemini-3.6-flash] 	"Indexed,X",
2026-08-13 07:55:29 [gemini-3.6-flash] 	"Relative"
2026-08-13 07:55:29 [gemini-3.6-flash] ]
2026-08-13 07:55:29 [gemini-3.6-flash] 
2026-08-13 07:55:29 [gemini-3.6-flash] 
2026-08-13 07:55:29 [gemini-3.6-flash] Addressing Mode Breakdown
2026-08-13 07:55:29 [gemini-3.6-flash] 
2026-08-13 07:55:29 [gemini-3.6-flash] 1. `Inherent` (or Implied/Accumulator): No memory operand required (e.g., `CLRA`, `INX`,
2026-08-13 07:55:29 [gemini-3.6-flash] `RTS`).
2026-08-13 07:55:29 [gemini-3.6-flash] 2. `Immediate`: 8-bit or 16-bit constant following opcode (e.g., `LDAA #$FF`).
2026-08-13 07:55:29 [gemini-3.6-flash] 3. `Direct`: 8-bit address targeting memory `0000`–`00FF` (Motorola's term for zero page).
2026-08-13 07:55:29 [gemini-3.6-flash] 4. `Extended`: Full 16-bit absolute address targeting `0000`–`FFFF` (equivalent to 6502
2026-08-13 07:55:29 [gemini-3.6-flash] `absolute`).
2026-08-13 07:55:29 [gemini-3.6-flash] 5. `Indexed,X`: 8-bit unsigned offset added to Index Register X.
2026-08-13 07:55:29 [gemini-3.6-flash] 6. `Relative`: 8-bit signed offset used exclusively by branch instructions.
2026-08-13 07:55:29 [gemini-3.6-flash] 
