2026-08-13 08:20:13 [grok-build-0.1] Key Observations
2026-08-13 08:20:13 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-08-13 08:20:13 [grok-build-0.1] - The Z80 has significantly more complexity than the 6502 or 6800. A full instruction set
2026-08-13 08:20:13 [grok-build-0.1] will need to handle:
2026-08-13 08:20:13 [grok-build-0.1]   - Unprefixed instructions
2026-08-13 08:20:13 [grok-build-0.1]   - `CB` prefix (bit operations)
2026-08-13 08:20:13 [grok-build-0.1]   - `DD` / `FD` prefixes (IX / IY indexed)
2026-08-13 08:20:13 [grok-build-0.1]   - `ED` prefix (extended instructions)
2026-08-13 08:20:13 [grok-build-0.1]   - Many instructions with multiple opcode lengths (1–4 bytes)
2026-08-13 08:20:13 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-08-13 08:20:13 [grok-build-0.1] - Your current 6502/6800 model uses a `"spec"` index into `specprofile` for byte/cycle counts. This
2026-08-13 08:20:13 [grok-build-0.1] approach will be much harder to apply cleanly to the Z80 because of the large number of
2026-08-13 08:20:13 [grok-build-0.1] timing variations and undocumented behaviors.
2026-08-13 08:20:13 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-08-13 08:20:13 [grok-build-0.1] - Z80 flags are different (`S`, `Z`, `H`, `P/V`, `N`, `C`). You'll need to decide how to represent
2026-08-13 08:20:13 [grok-build-0.1] the `P/V` flag (it serves as both Parity and Overflow).
2026-08-13 08:20:13 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-08-13 08:20:13 [grok-build-0.1] Recommendation
2026-08-13 08:20:14 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-08-13 08:20:14 [grok-build-0.1] If you want to keep consistency with your existing specs, the next logical steps would be to add:
2026-08-13 08:20:14 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-08-13 08:20:14 [grok-build-0.1] 1. Header fields (`copyright`, `license`, `repository`)
2026-08-13 08:20:14 [grok-build-0.1] 2. `flags` + `flagNames`
2026-08-13 08:20:14 [grok-build-0.1] 3. `addressmode` array (Z80 has quite a few)
2026-08-13 08:20:14 [grok-build-0.1] 4. A basic `instruction` skeleton
2026-08-13 08:20:14 [grok-build-0.1] 
