2026-08-13 08:42:48 [deepseek-v4-flash] For the Z80 `ADC` instruction, the supported addressing modes are:
2026-08-13 08:42:48 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-13 08:42:48 [deepseek-v4-flash] - Immediate – `ADC A, n`
2026-08-13 08:42:48 [deepseek-v4-flash] - Register – `ADC A, r` and `ADC HL, rr`
2026-08-13 08:42:48 [deepseek-v4-flash] - Register Indirect – `ADC A, (HL)`
2026-08-13 08:42:48 [deepseek-v4-flash] - Indexed – `ADC A, (IX+d)` and `ADC A, (IY+d)`
2026-08-13 08:42:48 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-13 08:42:48 [deepseek-v4-flash] So in your 10‑bit mask (bit positions as previously defined), the mask value would be:
2026-08-13 08:42:48 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-13 08:42:48 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-13 08:42:48 [deepseek-v4-flash] bits:  9 8 7 6 5 4 3 2 1 0
2026-08-13 08:42:48 [deepseek-v4-flash]        0 0 1 1 1 0 0 0 0 1
2026-08-13 08:42:48 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-13 08:42:48 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-13 08:42:48 [deepseek-v4-flash] Decimal: 225 (0b11100001, 0xE1).
2026-08-13 08:42:48 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-13 08:42:48 [deepseek-v4-flash] Breakdown of set bits:
2026-08-13 08:42:48 [deepseek-v4-flash] - bit 0 = immediate
2026-08-13 08:42:48 [deepseek-v4-flash] - bit 5 = indexed
2026-08-13 08:42:48 [deepseek-v4-flash] - bit 6 = register
2026-08-13 08:42:48 [deepseek-v4-flash] - bit 7 = register indirect
