2026-08-13 08:52:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.1 deepseek-v4-flash 🐋 🪠 0.7° $0.002 23.07KB 37.88s
2026-08-13 08:52:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] You're right to rename it — `opbits` conveys "operation bits with variable fields masked out" much
2026-08-13 08:52:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] better.
2026-08-13 08:52:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-13 08:52:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] For `ADC`, the set modes are:
2026-08-13 08:52:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] - immediate (bit 0)
2026-08-13 08:52:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] - indexed (bit 5)
2026-08-13 08:52:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] - register (bit 6)
2026-08-13 08:52:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] - register indirect (bit 7)
2026-08-13 08:52:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-13 08:52:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] If `opbits` is meant to be one entry per mode, that won't work for `ADC`, because two of
2026-08-13 08:52:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] those modes map to multiple distinct base encodings:
2026-08-13 08:52:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-13 08:52:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] ╭─────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────╮
2026-08-13 08:52:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] │  Mode               │  Encodings (register bits zeroed)  │
2026-08-13 08:52:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] ├─────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┤
2026-08-13 08:52:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] │  immediate          │  `CE`                              │
2026-08-13 08:52:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] │  register (8‑bit)   │  `88`   (low 3 bits = 0)           │
2026-08-13 08:52:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] │  register (16‑bit)  │  `ED 4A` (rr bits = 0)             │
2026-08-13 08:52:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] │  register indirect  │  `8E`                              │
2026-08-13 08:52:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] │  indexed            │  `DD 8E` (IX)                      │
2026-08-13 08:52:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] │  indexed            │  `FD 8E` (IY)                      │
2026-08-13 08:52:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] ╰─────────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────╯
2026-08-13 08:52:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-13 08:52:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] So there are 6 base patterns, not 4. A flat array with one byte per mode would lose
2026-08-13 08:52:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] important information.
2026-08-13 08:52:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-13 08:52:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] Instead, make `opbits` an array of objects that pair each mode with its masked base pattern(s):
2026-08-13 08:52:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-13 08:52:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-13 08:52:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] "ADC": {
2026-08-13 08:52:59 [deepseek-v4-flash]   "modes": "1000011100",
2026-08-13 08:52:59 [deepseek-v4-flash]   "opbits": [
2026-08-13 08:53:00 [deepseek-v4-flash]     { "mode": "immediate",         "base": "CE" },
2026-08-13 08:53:00 [deepseek-v4-flash]     { "mode": "register",          "base": "88" },
2026-08-13 08:53:00 [deepseek-v4-flash]     { "mode": "register",          "base": "ED 4A" },
2026-08-13 08:53:00 [deepseek-v4-flash]     { "mode": "register indirect", "base": "8E" },
2026-08-13 08:53:00 [deepseek-v4-flash]     { "mode": "indexed",           "base": "DD 8E" },
2026-08-13 08:53:00 [deepseek-v4-flash]     { "mode": "indexed",           "base": "FD 8E" }
2026-08-13 08:53:00 [deepseek-v4-flash]   ],
2026-08-13 08:53:00 [deepseek-v4-flash]   "label": "add with carry",
2026-08-13 08:53:00 [deepseek-v4-flash]   "flags": "SZHPNC"
2026-08-13 08:53:00 [deepseek-v4-flash] }
2026-08-13 08:53:00 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-13 08:53:00 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-13 08:53:00 [deepseek-v4-flash] Or, if you prefer a more compact nested object:
2026-08-13 08:53:00 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-13 08:53:00 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-13 08:53:00 [deepseek-v4-flash] "opbits": {
2026-08-13 08:53:00 [deepseek-v4-flash]   "immediate": ["CE"],
2026-08-13 08:53:00 [deepseek-v4-flash]   "register": ["88", "ED 4A"],
2026-08-13 08:53:00 [deepseek-v4-flash]   "register indirect": ["8E"],
2026-08-13 08:53:00 [deepseek-v4-flash]   "indexed": ["DD 8E", "FD 8E"]
2026-08-13 08:53:00 [deepseek-v4-flash] }
2026-08-13 08:53:00 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-13 08:53:00 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-13 08:53:00 [deepseek-v4-flash] Either way, the array length (6) now correctly reflects the distinct masked opcode patterns
2026-08-13 08:53:00 [deepseek-v4-flash] — which is why you can't equate it with the mode count (4).
2026-08-13 08:53:00 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
