2026-08-13 08:56:52 [deepseek-v4-flash] correctly captures both the 8‑bit register forms (`88` base) and the 16‑bit `HL` forms (`ED 4A`),
2026-08-13 08:56:52 [deepseek-v4-flash] plus both index prefixes (`DD`/`FD`).
2026-08-13 08:56:52 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-13 08:56:52 [deepseek-v4-flash] If you ever need the 10‑bit mask again, you can derive it from the object keys:
2026-08-13 08:56:52 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-13 08:56:52 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-13 08:56:52 [deepseek-v4-flash] immediate           → bit 0
2026-08-13 08:56:52 [deepseek-v4-flash] immediate extended  → bit 1
2026-08-13 08:56:52 [deepseek-v4-flash] modified page zero  → bit 2
2026-08-13 08:56:52 [deepseek-v4-flash] relative            → bit 3
2026-08-13 08:56:52 [deepseek-v4-flash] extended            → bit 4
2026-08-13 08:56:52 [deepseek-v4-flash] indexed             → bit 5
2026-08-13 08:56:52 [deepseek-v4-flash] register            → bit 6
2026-08-13 08:56:53 [deepseek-v4-flash] register indirect   → bit 7
2026-08-13 08:56:53 [deepseek-v4-flash] implied             → bit 8
2026-08-13 08:56:53 [deepseek-v4-flash] bit address         → bit 9
