2026-08-13 09:27:56 [deepseek-v4-flash]   "flags":"SZHPNC"
2026-08-13 09:27:56 [deepseek-v4-flash] }
2026-08-13 09:27:56 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-13 09:27:56 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-13 09:27:56 [deepseek-v4-flash] That's correct as a compact summary:
2026-08-13 09:27:57 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-13 09:27:57 [deepseek-v4-flash] - `CE` → `ADC A,n`
2026-08-13 09:27:57 [deepseek-v4-flash] - `88` → base for `ADC A,r` (register bits masked out)
2026-08-13 09:27:57 [deepseek-v4-flash] - `ED 4A` → base for `ADC HL,rr`
2026-08-13 09:27:57 [deepseek-v4-flash] - `8E` → `ADC A,(HL)`
2026-08-13 09:27:57 [deepseek-v4-flash] - `DD 8E` / `FD 8E` → `ADC A,(IX+d)` / `ADC A,(IY+d)`
2026-08-13 09:27:57 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-08-13 09:27:57 [deepseek-v4-flash] One thing to keep in mind: the `encoding` object in your z80.json currently covers only the
2026-08-13 09:27:57 [deepseek-v4-flash] base 256 opcodes. `CB`, `ED`, `DD`, `FD` are listed as markers, but their expanded
2026-08-13 09:27:57 [deepseek-v4-flash] sub‑opcodes are not included. That’s fine if `forms` is meant to be the authoritative source for
2026-08-13 09:27:57 [deepseek-v4-flash] instruction lookup; if you later want to generate disassembler tables, you’ll need to add the
2026-08-13 09:27:57 [deepseek-v4-flash] prefixed pages.
2026-08-13 09:27:57 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
