2026-08-16 07:19:46 [glm-5.2] 
2026-08-16 07:19:46 [glm-5.2] The opcodes, syntax, and cycle counts (T-states) all match the official Zilog timing tables:
2026-08-16 07:19:46 [glm-5.2] 
2026-08-16 07:19:46 [glm-5.2] • `ADC A, r` (registers) takes 4 T-states.
2026-08-16 07:19:46 [glm-5.2] • `ADC A, (HL)` takes 7 T-states.
2026-08-16 07:19:46 [glm-5.2] • `ADC A, n` (immediate) takes 7 T-states.
2026-08-16 07:19:46 [glm-5.2] • `ADC A, (IX+d)` / `ADC A, (IY+d)` take 19 T-states.
2026-08-16 07:19:46 [glm-5.2] • `ADC HL, rr` (16-bit register pairs) take 15 T-states.
2026-08-16 07:19:46 [glm-5.2] 
2026-08-16 07:19:46 [glm-5.2] The flag representation `"SZHPNC"` is also correct, as all `ADC` variants affect the Sign, Zero,
2026-08-16 07:19:46 [glm-5.2] Half-Carry, Parity/Overflow, Add/Subtract (N), and Carry flags.
2026-08-16 07:19:46 [glm-5.2] 
