2026-08-16 08:50:03 [glm-5.2] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.1 glm-5.2 Z 🪠 0.7° $0.007 570B 12.86s
2026-08-16 08:50:03 [glm-5.2] Hello. The Zilog Z80 microprocessor has a total of 22 registers. They are generally categorized as
2026-08-16 08:50:03 [glm-5.2] follows:
2026-08-16 08:50:03 [glm-5.2] 
2026-08-16 08:50:03 [glm-5.2] • Main Registers (8): A, F, B, C, D, E, H, and L. These are 8-bit registers, though they
2026-08-16 08:50:03 [glm-5.2] can be paired up (AF, BC, DE, HL) to perform 16-bit operations.
2026-08-16 08:50:03 [glm-5.2] • Shadow Registers (8): A', F', B', C', D', E', H', and L'. These are alternate versions of
2026-08-16 08:50:03 [glm-5.2] the main registers. They cannot be addressed directly, but contents can be exchanged with the main
2026-08-16 08:50:03 [glm-5.2] registers using specific instructions, which is useful for fast context switching during
2026-08-16 08:50:03 [glm-5.2] interrupts.
2026-08-16 08:50:03 [glm-5.2] • Index Registers (2): IX and IY. These are 16-bit registers used primarily for indexed
2026-08-16 08:50:03 [glm-5.2] addressing modes.
