2026-08-16 14:07:35 [glm-5.2] 
2026-08-16 14:07:35 [glm-5.2] - Row 0, col 2 is `0x27` (VK_RIGHT). On the C64 matrix that position is Right Shift, which
2026-08-16 14:07:35 [glm-5.2] is usually `0xA1` (VK_RSHIFT). VK_RIGHT currently lives here, and VK_DOWN (`0x28`) is in col 7, so
2026-08-16 14:07:35 [glm-5.2] the two cursor arrows are split across the row.
2026-08-16 14:07:35 [glm-5.2] - Row 6 contains duplicates of codes already used elsewhere: `0x74` (F5), `0x70` (F1) and
2026-08-16 14:07:35 [glm-5.2] `0xBB` (OEM_PLUS) all reappear. The canonical C64 row 6 is `£, *, ;, HOME, =, ↑/PI, /, RUN‑STOP`,
2026-08-16 14:07:35 [glm-5.2] so this row looks like it may have drifted — for example `0x1B` (Escape) is in col 2 where `;`
2026-08-16 14:07:35 [glm-5.2] would be expected, and `0x24` (Home) is in col 4 where `=` would be expected.
