2026-08-17 08:53:56 [nitro@ryzen5] on vic20 is runstop key special?
2026-08-17 08:54:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.1 gemini-3.7-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.004 497B 5.82s
2026-08-17 08:54:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] Yes, the RUN/STOP key is quite special on the Commodore VIC-20, serving as a primary
2026-08-17 08:54:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] control key for both the operating system (KERNAL) and BASIC environment.
2026-08-17 08:54:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-17 08:54:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] Here are the main ways it functions:
2026-08-17 08:54:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-17 08:54:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 1. Halting Program Execution
2026-08-17 08:54:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] Pressed on its own while a BASIC program is executing, it immediately interrupts the program and
2026-08-17 08:54:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] returns control to the user, displaying a `BREAK IN LINE [X]` message.
2026-08-17 08:54:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-17 08:54:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 2. Auto-Loading from Tape (`SHIFT` + `RUN/STOP`)
2026-08-17 08:54:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] When pressed in combination with the SHIFT key, it acts as a shortcut to load and run the
2026-08-17 08:54:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] next program from a connected Commodore Datassette tape drive. It automatically prints `LOAD` to
2026-08-17 08:54:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] the screen, prompts the user to press PLAY on the tape unit, and automatically executes `RUN` once
2026-08-17 08:54:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] loading finishes.
2026-08-17 08:54:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-17 08:54:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 3. Warm Reset (`RUN/STOP` + `RESTORE`)
2026-08-17 08:54:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] When held down while pressing the RESTORE key, it triggers a Non-Maskable Interrupt (NMI)
2026-08-17 08:54:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] on the 6502 processor. This performs a "warm reset," which:
2026-08-17 08:54:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Clears the screen and resets text colors to default.
2026-08-17 08:54:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Silences the sound registers.
2026-08-17 08:54:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Returns the system to the `READY.` prompt while preserving the BASIC program currently in
2026-08-17 08:54:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] memory.
2026-08-17 08:54:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-17 08:54:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 4. Software Control and Trapping
