2026-08-17 09:07:07 [gemini-3.7-flash] Looking at the VIC-20 hardware matrix (VIA #1 / VIA #2):
2026-08-17 09:07:07 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-17 09:07:07 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Left Shift is physically wired to Row 3, Column 1.
2026-08-17 09:07:07 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Right Shift is physically wired to Row 4, Column 6.
2026-08-17 09:07:07 [gemini-3.7-flash] • RUN/STOP is physically wired to Row 7, Column 7 (or Row 3, Column 0 depending on
2026-08-17 09:07:07 [gemini-3.7-flash] bit polarity).
2026-08-17 09:07:07 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-17 09:07:07 [gemini-3.7-flash] In your original array:
2026-08-17 09:07:07 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Row 4 started with `0xBA` where RUN/STOP should have been.
2026-08-17 09:07:07 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Row 5 ended with `0xBA` where Function Key (F1) should have been.
