2026-08-18 07:21:23 [gemini-3.7-flash] On the Commodore PET, `$E810` (PIA 1, Port A) is connected directly to the keyboard
2026-08-18 07:21:23 [gemini-3.7-flash] matrix return lines.
2026-08-18 07:21:23 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 07:21:24 [gemini-3.7-flash] Bit Layout for `$E810` (Read Mode)
2026-08-18 07:21:24 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 07:21:24 [gemini-3.7-flash] All 8 bits (Bits 0 through 7) are configured as inputs to sense the keyboard columns:
2026-08-18 07:21:24 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 07:21:24 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Bit 0 (`PA0`): Keyboard Column 0
2026-08-18 07:21:24 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Bit 1 (`PA1`): Keyboard Column 1
2026-08-18 07:21:24 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Bit 2 (`PA2`): Keyboard Column 2
2026-08-18 07:21:24 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Bit 3 (`PA3`): Keyboard Column 3
2026-08-18 07:21:24 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Bit 4 (`PA4`): Keyboard Column 4
2026-08-18 07:21:24 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Bit 5 (`PA5`): Keyboard Column 5
2026-08-18 07:21:24 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Bit 6 (`PA6`): Keyboard Column 6
2026-08-18 07:21:24 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Bit 7 (`PA7`): Keyboard Column 7
2026-08-18 07:21:24 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 07:21:24 [gemini-3.7-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-08-18 07:21:24 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 07:21:24 [gemini-3.7-flash] How the Hardware Reads It
2026-08-18 07:21:24 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 07:21:24 [gemini-3.7-flash] 1. Row Selection: The kernel writes a 4-bit row index (0–9) to `$E812` (PIA 1, Port B,
2026-08-18 07:21:24 [gemini-3.7-flash] bits 0–3). This feeds a 74145 BCD-to-decimal decoder, which pulls the selected matrix row low.
2026-08-18 07:21:24 [gemini-3.7-flash] 2. Column Sensing: The kernel reads `$E810` to see which keys in that row are
2026-08-18 07:21:24 [gemini-3.7-flash] pressed.
2026-08-18 07:21:24 [gemini-3.7-flash] 3. Logic Levels:
2026-08-18 07:21:24 [gemini-3.7-flash]    * `1` (High): Key is not pressed (held high by pull-up resistors).
2026-08-18 07:21:24 [gemini-3.7-flash]    * `0` (Low): Key is pressed (pulled to ground through the selected row).
2026-08-18 07:21:24 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 07:21:24 [gemini-3.7-flash] If no keys are pressed on the keyboard, reading `E810` should return `FF`.
