2026-08-18 08:48:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] This loop is the PET Editor ROM's `CHRIN` / `BASIN` line input wait loop.
2026-08-18 08:48:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 08:48:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] What the Code is Doing
2026-08-18 08:48:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 08:48:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] 1. Wait State: Location `$020D` acts as the input line length / Return flag for the
2026-08-18 08:48:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] screen editor.
2026-08-18 08:48:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] 2. The Loop: While `020D` is `0`, no completed line (terminated by the `RETURN` key) is
2026-08-18 08:48:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] ready for BASIC to process. The routine continuously loops at `E297`, waiting for input.
2026-08-18 08:48:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] 3. Exit Condition: When the user types a command and presses `RETURN`, the editor updates
2026-08-18 08:48:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] `020D` with the number of characters in the current logical screen line. The loop then branches
2026-08-18 08:48:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] past `E29D` so BASIC can read and evaluate the input.
2026-08-18 08:48:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 08:48:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
