2026-08-18 08:48:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] What This Means for Your Simulator
2026-08-18 08:48:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 08:48:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] • If the startup banner (` COMMODORE BASIC `, memory size, `READY.`) is visible
2026-08-18 08:48:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] on the screen:
2026-08-18 08:48:52 [gemini-3.7-flash]   Your simulator has successfully booted. The CPU is idling at the `READY.` prompt, waiting for
2026-08-18 08:48:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] user keyboard input.
2026-08-18 08:48:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 08:48:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] • If the screen is still blank or no prompt appeared:
2026-08-18 08:48:52 [gemini-3.7-flash]   1. Hardware IRQ Timer: Ensure your simulator is generating periodic interrupts (the ~60
2026-08-18 08:48:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] Hz PIA 1 / VIA timer tick). The IRQ service routine is responsible for blinking the cursor and
2026-08-18 08:48:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] scanning keyboard matrix lines.
2026-08-18 08:48:52 [gemini-3.7-flash]   2. Keyboard Matrix Simulation: When simulating key presses, ensure the keyboard scan
2026-08-18 08:48:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] routine receives the key matrix changes at `E810` / `E812` so it can populate the keyboard buffer.
