2026-08-18 17:38:43 [gemini-3.7-flash] The Problem
2026-08-18 17:38:43 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 17:38:43 [gemini-3.7-flash] 1. Active Low Lines: When no keys are pressed, the lines are pulled HIGH (`$FF`).
2026-08-18 17:38:43 [gemini-3.7-flash] When a key is pressed, it pulls the corresponding line LOW (`0`).
2026-08-18 17:38:43 [gemini-3.7-flash] 2. Port Assignments on PET:
2026-08-18 17:38:43 [gemini-3.7-flash]    * `PIA1_PA` (`$E810`) is driven by the CPU as an output to select which keyboard
2026-08-18 17:38:43 [gemini-3.7-flash] row to scan (via a 74145 BCD-to-decimal decoder).
2026-08-18 17:38:43 [gemini-3.7-flash]    * `PIA1_PB` (`$E812`) is configured as an input to read the 8 column lines
2026-08-18 17:38:43 [gemini-3.7-flash] returning from the keyboard matrix.
2026-08-18 17:38:43 [gemini-3.7-flash] 3. What Happened in Your Emulator:
2026-08-18 17:38:43 [gemini-3.7-flash]    * Your code returned `$FF` for `0xE810` (`PIA1_PA`), but let `0xE812` (`PIA1_PB`) fall through
2026-08-18 17:38:43 [gemini-3.7-flash] to return `mem[0xE812]`, which was initialized to `0x00`.
2026-08-18 17:38:43 [gemini-3.7-flash]    * Because `PIA1_PB` returned `0x00`, the Kernal thought all 8 column lines were grounded (every
2026-08-18 17:38:43 [gemini-3.7-flash] key pressed).
