2026-08-18 17:54:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] In the PET's screen character set (Screen Codes):
2026-08-18 17:54:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 17:54:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] • `$00` represents the `@` character.
2026-08-18 17:54:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] • `$20` represents a Space (` `).
2026-08-18 17:54:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 17:54:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] Screen Codes vs. PETSCII
2026-08-18 17:54:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] The Commodore PET does not store standard PETSCII/ASCII directly in video RAM (`8000–83E7`).
2026-08-18 17:54:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] Instead, the hardware character generator ROM is indexed using Screen Codes:
2026-08-18 17:54:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 17:54:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] ╭─────────────┬─────────────────────┬─────────────────╮
2026-08-18 17:54:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] │  Character  │  Screen Code (Hex)  │  PETSCII (Hex)  │
2026-08-18 17:54:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] ├─────────────┼─────────────────────┼─────────────────┤
2026-08-18 17:54:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] │  :---       │  :---               │  :---           │
2026-08-18 17:54:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] │  **`@`**    │  **`$00`**          │  `$40`          │
2026-08-18 17:54:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] │  `A`        │  `$01`              │  `$41`          │
2026-08-18 17:54:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] │  `B`        │  `$02`              │  `$42`          │
2026-08-18 17:54:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] │  ...        │  ...                │  ...            │
2026-08-18 17:54:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] │  **Space**  │  **`$20`**          │  **`$20`**      │
2026-08-18 17:54:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] ╰─────────────┴─────────────────────┴─────────────────╯
2026-08-18 17:54:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 17:54:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] Because video RAM filled with `00` displays as a screen full of `@` symbols (often seen briefly on
2026-08-18 17:54:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] real hardware at power-up before the Kernal executes the screen-clear routine), the PET Kernal will
2026-08-18 17:54:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] soon write `20` to the entire 1000-byte video buffer to blank/clear the display before printing the
2026-08-18 17:54:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] startup banner.
2026-08-18 17:54:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
