2026-08-18 17:56:33 [gemini-3.7-flash] What is Being Copied:
2026-08-18 17:56:33 [gemini-3.7-flash] In Microsoft 6502 BASIC (including Commodore BASIC 1.0/2.0/4.0), the fundamental character-getting
2026-08-18 17:56:33 [gemini-3.7-flash] subroutine `CHRGET` (and `CHRGOT`) is copied directly into Zero Page RAM starting at `0070`
2026-08-18 17:56:33 [gemini-3.7-flash] (or `00C1` in this specific PET ROM revision layout).
2026-08-18 17:56:33 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 17:56:33 [gemini-3.7-flash] Because `CHRGET` is executed for almost every byte of BASIC text parsed during program execution,
2026-08-18 17:56:33 [gemini-3.7-flash] running it out of zero page allows the code to use fast Zero-Page addressing and self-modifying
2026-08-18 17:56:33 [gemini-3.7-flash] pointers (`INC $xx` / `BNE`).
2026-08-18 17:56:33 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 17:56:33 [gemini-3.7-flash] Breakdown of the Opcodes Being Copied:
2026-08-18 17:56:33 [gemini-3.7-flash] The bytes copied in this trace comprise the core text scanning and numeric-validation logic:
2026-08-18 17:56:33 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 17:56:33 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 17:56:33 [gemini-3.7-flash] ; Bytes being written to zero page:
2026-08-18 17:56:33 [gemini-3.7-flash] $CB: CMP #$3A      ; C9 3A    - Check if character is ':' (statement separator) or > '9'
2026-08-18 17:56:33 [gemini-3.7-flash] $CD: BCS ...       ; B0 ...   - Branch if >= ':' (not a digit)
2026-08-18 17:56:33 [gemini-3.7-flash] $CF: CMP #$20      ; C9 20    - Check if character is a space
2026-08-18 17:56:33 [gemini-3.7-flash] $D1: BEQ ...       ; F0 ...   - Skip spaces automatically
2026-08-18 17:56:33 [gemini-3.7-flash] $D3: SEC           ; 38       - Prepare Carry for subtraction
2026-08-18 17:56:33 [gemini-3.7-flash] $D4: SBC #$30      ; E9 30    - Convert ASCII/PETSCII digit ('0'-'9') to binary value
2026-08-18 17:56:33 [gemini-3.7-flash] $D6: SEC           ; 38
2026-08-18 17:56:33 [gemini-3.7-flash] $D7: SBC #$D0      ; E9 D0    - Validate range / carry flag state
2026-08-18 17:56:33 [gemini-3.7-flash] $D9: RTS           ; 60       - Return to caller with character in A and status flags set
