2026-08-18 18:16:48 [gemini-3.7-flash] On the Commodore PET, VIA PB5 (`$E840`, Bit 5) is connected specifically to the
2026-08-18 18:16:48 [gemini-3.7-flash] Combined Video Blanking / Retrace signal coming from the discrete video timing logic (or
2026-08-18 18:16:48 [gemini-3.7-flash] the CRTC in later models), but in terms of timing, it checks both horizontal and vertical
2026-08-18 18:16:48 [gemini-3.7-flash] blanking:
2026-08-18 18:16:48 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 18:16:48 [gemini-3.7-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-08-18 18:16:48 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 18:16:48 [gemini-3.7-flash] Hardware Details
2026-08-18 18:16:48 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 18:16:48 [gemini-3.7-flash] 1. The Circuit Connection:
2026-08-18 18:16:48 [gemini-3.7-flash]    * On original dynamic-board PETs (e.g., 2001, 2001-N, 3032, early 4032s), the PET uses discrete
2026-08-18 18:16:48 [gemini-3.7-flash] TTL counters (like 74LS163 / 74LS74) to generate video timing.
2026-08-18 18:16:48 [gemini-3.7-flash]    * The hardware combines Horizontal Blanking (\sim16\text–20\ μ\texts per scanline) and
2026-08-18 18:16:48 [gemini-3.7-flash] Vertical Blanking (\sim1.2\text–1.5\text ms per field) into a single master composite
2026-08-18 18:16:48 [gemini-3.7-flash] `BLANK` (or `RETRACE`) line.
2026-08-18 18:16:48 [gemini-3.7-flash]    * This master blanking line is tied to VIA Pin 15 (Port B, Bit 5).
2026-08-18 18:16:48 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 18:16:48 [gemini-3.7-flash] 2. Why Horizontal Retrace is Critical for Single-Character Writes:
2026-08-18 18:16:48 [gemini-3.7-flash]     Vertical blanking only happens 50/60 times per second (once every \sim16.6\text ms
2026-08-18 18:16:48 [gemini-3.7-flash] or 20\text ms). If the Kernal waited for a vertical blank on every single character* printed,
2026-08-18 18:16:48 [gemini-3.7-flash] printing a 40-character line would take almost a full second.
2026-08-18 18:16:48 [gemini-3.7-flash]    * Instead, by syncing to the blanking line, the tight two-instruction loop (`LDA E840` / `AND
2026-08-18 18:16:48 [gemini-3.7-flash] #20` / `BNE`) catches the next Horizontal Blanking interval (which occurs roughly every 64\
2026-08-18 18:16:48 [gemini-3.7-flash] μ\texts).
2026-08-18 18:16:48 [gemini-3.7-flash]    * As soon as the electron beam hits the right margin and turns off to travel back left, the CPU
2026-08-18 18:16:48 [gemini-3.7-flash] writes the character to video RAM before the beam starts drawing the next scanline.
2026-08-18 18:16:48 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 18:16:48 [gemini-3.7-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-08-18 18:16:48 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 18:16:48 [gemini-3.7-flash] In Summary
2026-08-18 18:16:48 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Interrupts (Timer / 60 Hz system clock): Synced to Vertical Sync (via PIA1 CB1 /
2026-08-18 18:16:48 [gemini-3.7-flash] VIA CB2).
2026-08-18 18:16:49 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Character Screen Writes (`VIA_ORB` Bit 5 at `$E7AD`): Checks the composite
2026-08-18 18:16:49 [gemini-3.7-flash] Blanking signal, which allows each individual character write to slip into the next
2026-08-18 18:16:49 [gemini-3.7-flash] available Horizontal Retrace without stalling the CPU.
2026-08-18 18:16:49 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
