2026-08-18 18:42:18 [gemini-3.7-flash] There are a few common reasons why the execution trace indicates writes are occurring at an address
2026-08-18 18:42:18 [gemini-3.7-flash] (such as `$8328`) while the memory dump shows the data was not modified:
2026-08-18 18:42:18 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 18:42:18 [gemini-3.7-flash] 1. Address Decoding and Bus Routing in `writeAddress`
2026-08-18 18:42:18 [gemini-3.7-flash] If `writeAddress(address, value)` contains memory mapping logic (such as bank switching, RAM/ROM
2026-08-18 18:42:18 [gemini-3.7-flash] tables, or hardware registers):
2026-08-18 18:42:18 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Ensure the target range (around `$8000`) is mapped as writable RAM. If the address maps to a ROM
2026-08-18 18:42:18 [gemini-3.7-flash] area or an unmapped region in your memory controller, `writeAddress` may be silently dropping the
2026-08-18 18:42:18 [gemini-3.7-flash] value.
2026-08-18 18:42:18 [gemini-3.7-flash] • If `writeAddress` writes to a dedicated video RAM buffer or a banked array instead of the main
2026-08-18 18:42:18 [gemini-3.7-flash] `this.memory` array, direct inspection of `this.memory` will not reflect the changes.
2026-08-18 18:42:18 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 18:42:18 [gemini-3.7-flash] 2. Discrepancy Between Memory Dump Method and Write Method
2026-08-18 18:42:18 [gemini-3.7-flash] • If your memory dump inspects `this.memory[...]` directly rather than invoking your system's read
2026-08-18 18:42:18 [gemini-3.7-flash] method (e.g. `this.readAddress(...)`), any banking, mirroring, or memory controller translation
2026-08-18 18:42:18 [gemini-3.7-flash] used during execution will cause the dump to show the wrong physical backing array.
2026-08-18 18:42:18 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 18:42:18 [gemini-3.7-flash] 3. Direct Zero-Page Access
2026-08-18 18:42:18 [gemini-3.7-flash] In the opcode implementation, the pointer bytes are read directly from `this.memory[base]` rather
2026-08-18 18:42:18 [gemini-3.7-flash] than via `this.readAddress(base)` or `this.get8(base)`. If zero-page memory is banked, offset, or
2026-08-18 18:42:18 [gemini-3.7-flash] mirrored, reading `this.memory` directly might fetch incorrect pointer addresses compared to
2026-08-18 18:42:18 [gemini-3.7-flash] standard bus reads.
2026-08-18 18:42:18 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 18:42:18 [gemini-3.7-flash] 4. Overwriting by Subsequent Operations
2026-08-18 18:42:18 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Check if a subsequent interrupt handler, display refresh routine, or DMA cycle runs immediately
2026-08-18 18:42:18 [gemini-3.7-flash] after this loop and resets the video memory.
