2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.1 gemini-3.7-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.007 513B 8.94s
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] On the Commodore PET, the memory address `$E811` corresponds to the Control Register A
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] (CRA) of the primary MOS 6520 Peripheral Interface Adapter (PIA 1).
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] The value of this register is determined by a combination of software configuration and hardware
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] state changes.
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] 1. Software-Written Bits (Bits 0–5)
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] Bits 0 through 5 are written directly by the CPU to configure the PIA's operating mode:
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Bit 0 (CA1 Interrupt Enable):
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash]   * `0`: Disables IRQ generation from the CA1 line.
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash]   * `1`: Enables IRQ generation to the 6502 when the CA1 interrupt condition occurs.
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Bit 1 (CA1 Active Transition Select):
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash]   * `0`: Detects a high-to-low (falling edge) transition on CA1.
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash]   * `1`: Detects a low-to-high (rising edge) transition on CA1.
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Bit 2 (Data Direction Register Access):
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash]   * `0`: Directs reads/writes at `$E810` to the Data Direction Register A (DDRA).
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash]   * `1`: Directs reads/writes at `$E810` to the Port A Output Register / Input Pins (PRA).
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Bits 3, 4, and 5 (CA2 Control):
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash]   * Configure the operation of the CA2 line (e.g., input interrupt mode, pulse output mode, or
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] fixed manual output level).
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] 2. Hardware-Driven Status Flags (Bits 6 & 7)
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] Bits 6 and 7 are read-only flags set directly by electrical transitions on the external control
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] pins:
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Bit 6 (IRQA2 Flag):
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash]   * Set to `1` by an active transition on the CA2 line when configured as an input.
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash]   * On most PET mainboards, CA2 is commonly configured by the ROM as an output to control the
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] Cassette #1 Motor line, keeping this flag inactive during standard operation.
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Bit 7 (IRQA1 Flag):
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash]   * Set to `1` when an active edge occurs on the CA1 line.
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash]   * On the PET hardware, the CA1 line is physically connected to the Cassette #1 Read
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] Data line. Pulses coming from the tape read head toggle this flag.
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] 3. Reset and Clearing Behavior
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Reset: A hardware reset clears the entire register to `$00`.
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Clearing Flags: Reading the associated Port A data register (`$E810`) automatically
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] resets Bits 6 and 7 back to `0`.
2026-08-19 08:17:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
