2026-08-19 08:30:17 [gemini-3.7-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.1 gemini-3.7-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.045 166.4KB 4.65s
2026-08-19 08:30:17 [gemini-3.7-flash] On the Commodore PET, address `$E810` connects to the MOS 6520 PIA 1 (Port A
2026-08-19 08:30:17 [gemini-3.7-flash] data/direction register).
2026-08-19 08:30:17 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 08:30:17 [gemini-3.7-flash] What it returns depends directly on Bit 2 of the Control Register A (`$E811`) and the
2026-08-19 08:30:17 [gemini-3.7-flash] hardware lines connected to Port A:
2026-08-19 08:30:17 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 08:30:17 [gemini-3.7-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-08-19 08:30:17 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 08:30:17 [gemini-3.7-flash] 1. When Bit 2 of `$E811` = 0 (Data Direction Register Access)
2026-08-19 08:30:17 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Returns: The contents of DDRA (Data Direction Register A).
2026-08-19 08:30:17 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Behavior: Whatever value the CPU previously wrote to `E810` while `CRA bit 2 == 0`.
2026-08-19 08:30:17 [gemini-3.7-flash] (During boot, the PET Kernal configures the lower 4 bits as outputs to drive the 74145 column
2026-08-19 08:30:17 [gemini-3.7-flash] decoder, so DDRA is typically `3F` or `$0F`).
