2026-08-19 08:30:17 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Returns: The combined state of the Port A Output Register and the Physical
2026-08-19 08:30:17 [gemini-3.7-flash] Input Pins (PRA).
2026-08-19 08:30:17 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Reading Port A also clears the interrupt flags in `$E811` (Bits 6 & 7 reset to `0`).
2026-08-19 08:30:17 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 08:30:17 [gemini-3.7-flash] Physical Pin Mapping on the PET:
2026-08-19 08:30:17 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Bits 0–3 (PA0–PA3): Configured as Outputs
2026-08-19 08:30:17 [gemini-3.7-flash]   * Drive the 74145 BCD-to-Decimal Keyboard Column Decoder.
2026-08-19 08:30:17 [gemini-3.7-flash]   * Reading these bits returns the last value written by software to `$E810` (the active
2026-08-19 08:30:17 [gemini-3.7-flash] column nibble, e.g., `0x0` through `0x9`, or `0xF` when disabled).
2026-08-19 08:30:17 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Bits 4–5 (PA4–PA5): Outputs / Diagnostics
2026-08-19 08:30:17 [gemini-3.7-flash]   * Used for cassette motor control / IEEE-488 diagnostic lines.
2026-08-19 08:30:17 [gemini-3.7-flash]   * Reading these bits returns the last software output state (or `1`s via pull-up resistors if
2026-08-19 08:30:17 [gemini-3.7-flash] unconfigured).
2026-08-19 08:30:17 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Bits 6–7 (PA6–PA7): Configured as Inputs
2026-08-19 08:30:17 [gemini-3.7-flash]   * Connected to the IEEE-488 control lines (specifically `EOI` and `NDAC`/Cassette Sense
2026-08-19 08:30:17 [gemini-3.7-flash] depending on board revisions).
2026-08-19 08:30:17 [gemini-3.7-flash]   * With no IEEE devices attached, these float high due to internal pull-up resistors
2026-08-19 08:30:17 [gemini-3.7-flash] (`1`).
