2026-08-19 08:41:29 [gemini-3.7-flash] The Root Cause: `INC $E810` on PIA1 Port A
2026-08-19 08:41:29 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 08:41:29 [gemini-3.7-flash] In the trace during the keyboard scan routine:
2026-08-19 08:41:30 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 08:41:30 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 08:41:30 [gemini-3.7-flash] E6C0: STA $E810       ; Writes $F0 to select Column 0
2026-08-19 08:41:30 [gemini-3.7-flash] ...
2026-08-19 08:41:30 [gemini-3.7-flash] E6F9: LDA $E812       ; Reads row inputs for current column
2026-08-19 08:41:30 [gemini-3.7-flash] ...
2026-08-19 08:41:30 [gemini-3.7-flash] E70F: INC $E810       ; Increments column counter ($F0 -> $F1 for column 1)
2026-08-19 08:41:30 [gemini-3.7-flash] E712: BNE $E6F7       ; Loop back to scan next column if not zero
2026-08-19 08:41:30 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 08:41:30 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 08:41:30 [gemini-3.7-flash] The Kernal uses `INC E810` (a read-modify-write instruction) to step through columns `F0` through
2026-08-19 08:41:30 [gemini-3.7-flash] `$F9`.
2026-08-19 08:41:30 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 08:41:30 [gemini-3.7-flash] In `Machine.readPET`:
2026-08-19 08:41:30 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 08:41:30 [gemini-3.7-flash] case 0xe810: // kb matrix
2026-08-19 08:41:30 [gemini-3.7-flash] 	mem[0xE811] &= 0x3f;
2026-08-19 08:41:30 [gemini-3.7-flash] 	return 0xff;
2026-08-19 08:41:30 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 08:41:30 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 08:41:30 [gemini-3.7-flash] When `INC $E810` executes:
2026-08-19 08:41:30 [gemini-3.7-flash] 1. `readAddress(0xE810)` is called, which returns the hardcoded value `0xFF`.
2026-08-19 08:41:30 [gemini-3.7-flash] 2. The 6502 increments `0xFF` to `0x00`.
2026-08-19 08:41:30 [gemini-3.7-flash] 3. The Zero flag (Z) is set to `1`.
2026-08-19 08:41:30 [gemini-3.7-flash] 4. `E712: BNE` sees Z = 1 and fails to branch, terminating the loop immediately after
2026-08-19 08:41:30 [gemini-3.7-flash] Column 0.
2026-08-19 08:41:30 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 08:41:30 [gemini-3.7-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-08-19 08:41:30 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 08:41:30 [gemini-3.7-flash] What `$E297` Is Doing
2026-08-19 08:41:30 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 08:41:30 [gemini-3.7-flash] The loop at the bottom of your trace:
2026-08-19 08:41:30 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 08:41:30 [gemini-3.7-flash] E297: LDA $020D       ; Read number of characters in keyboard buffer (NDX)
2026-08-19 08:41:30 [gemini-3.7-flash] E29A: STA $0224       ; Enable cursor blinking when buffer is empty
2026-08-19 08:41:30 [gemini-3.7-flash] E29D: BEQ $E297       ; Loop waiting for keypress
2026-08-19 08:41:30 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 08:41:30 [gemini-3.7-flash] This is the PET Kernal's idle cursor-blink / `GETIN` loop waiting for characters in the keyboard
2026-08-19 08:41:30 [gemini-3.7-flash] buffer. Because `INC $E810` wrapped to zero and terminated column scanning, keys typed on other
2026-08-19 08:41:30 [gemini-3.7-flash] columns were never detected.
