2026-08-19 12:41:25 [glm-5.3] block is labelled `LAX (Indirect), X` and implemented as 2-byte indirect,X, but `AF` on real
2026-08-19 12:41:25 [glm-5.3] silicon is LAX absolute (3 bytes) — indirect,X is `A3`. The opcode table entry describing
2026-08-19 12:41:25 [glm-5.3] it as a 2-byte LDA would also want correcting at the same time.
2026-08-19 12:41:25 [glm-5.3] 
