2026-08-19 16:35:28 [gemini-3.7-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.1 gemini-3.7-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.013 4.089KB 11.23s
2026-08-19 16:35:28 [gemini-3.7-flash] Here is an analysis of the implementation, highlighting the key 6520 PIA and 6522 VIA behaviours
2026-08-19 16:35:28 [gemini-3.7-flash] that need adjustments.
2026-08-19 16:35:28 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 16:35:28 [gemini-3.7-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-08-19 16:35:28 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 16:35:28 [gemini-3.7-flash] Key Areas to Address
2026-08-19 16:35:28 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 16:35:28 [gemini-3.7-flash] 1. Missing DDRB handling on PIA 1 (`E812` / `E813`)
2026-08-19 16:35:28 [gemini-3.7-flash] • On the 6520 PIA, Port B uses the exact same multiplexing mechanism as Port A.
2026-08-19 16:35:28 [gemini-3.7-flash] • When bit 2 of `CRB` (`E813`) is `0`, `E812` accesses the Data Direction Register B (`DDRB`).
2026-08-19 16:35:28 [gemini-3.7-flash] • When bit 2 of `CRB` is `1`, `$E812` accesses the Output/Input Register B.
2026-08-19 16:35:28 [gemini-3.7-flash] • The PET startup ROM initializes both `DDRA` and `DDRB`. Without `ddrb` handling, writes to
2026-08-19 16:35:28 [gemini-3.7-flash] configure Port B may be lost.
2026-08-19 16:35:28 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 16:35:28 [gemini-3.7-flash] 2. Interrupt Flag Clearing (Bits 6 & 7)
2026-08-19 16:35:28 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Reading the peripheral data register (`PRA` / `PRB`) clears the interrupt flags in the respective
2026-08-19 16:35:28 [gemini-3.7-flash] control register (`CRA` / `CRB`).
2026-08-19 16:35:28 [gemini-3.7-flash] • However, reading the Direction Register (`DDRA` / `DDRB`) must not clear the interrupt
