2026-08-19 17:58:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] Yes, during a normal ROM keyboard scan interrupt, you should see writes to `E810` cycling through
2026-08-19 17:58:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] values `0` through `9` (and then typically `0F` or `$00` when done).
2026-08-19 17:58:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 17:58:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] Here is the exact mechanism inside the Commodore PET Kernal ROM:
2026-08-19 17:58:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 17:58:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-08-19 17:58:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 17:58:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] How the PET Kernal Scans the Keyboard
2026-08-19 17:58:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 17:58:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 1. Outer Loop: The Kernal IRQ routine initializes a row/column counter (typically starting
2026-08-19 17:58:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] at `0` or `9`).
2026-08-19 17:58:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 2. Select Row: It writes the 4-bit number to Port A:
2026-08-19 17:58:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 17:58:04 [gemini-3.7-flash]    STA $E810       ; Outputs row 0..9 to 74145 BCD decoder
2026-08-19 17:58:04 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 17:58:04 [gemini-3.7-flash] 3. Read Columns: It immediately reads Port B:
2026-08-19 17:58:04 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 17:58:04 [gemini-3.7-flash]    LDA $E812       ; Reads the 8 column lines for the active row
2026-08-19 17:58:04 [gemini-3.7-flash]    CMP #$FF        ; $FF means no keys pressed on this row
2026-08-19 17:58:04 [gemini-3.7-flash]    BNE .key_found  ; If not $FF, a key is down on this row!
2026-08-19 17:58:04 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 17:58:04 [gemini-3.7-flash] 4. Loop: It increments (or decrements) the counter and repeats until all 10 rows (0
2026-08-19 17:58:04 [gemini-3.7-flash] through 9) have been tested.
2026-08-19 17:58:04 [gemini-3.7-flash] 5. Deselect: After the loop completes, it usually writes an invalid BCD digit (like `$0F`)
2026-08-19 17:58:04 [gemini-3.7-flash] to turn off all 74145 outputs.
2026-08-19 17:58:04 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 17:58:04 [gemini-3.7-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-08-19 17:58:04 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
