2026-08-19 17:58:04 [gemini-3.7-flash] Potential Reasons It Only Scans One Column or None
2026-08-19 17:58:04 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 17:58:04 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Port B Returning Non-`$FF` on Idle:
2026-08-19 17:58:04 [gemini-3.7-flash]   If `readPetMatrix()` returns `0x00` (or anything other than `0xFF`) when no keys are pressed, the
2026-08-19 17:58:04 [gemini-3.7-flash] Kernal believes every key on row 0 is pressed. Depending on the ROM version, it may either
2026-08-19 17:58:04 [gemini-3.7-flash] branch early to debounce/handle the key or lock up the scan.
2026-08-19 17:58:04 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Bit 7 of `$E813` (CRB) Not Set:
2026-08-19 17:58:04 [gemini-3.7-flash]   If bit 7 of `$E813` is not asserted when the IRQ fires, the Kernal interrupt handler treats the
2026-08-19 17:58:04 [gemini-3.7-flash] IRQ as a timer or cassette interrupt and skips the keyboard scanning loop entirely.
2026-08-19 17:58:04 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Interrupt Flag Cleared Prematurely:
2026-08-19 17:58:04 [gemini-3.7-flash]   If `E812` is read somewhere outside the IRQ routine, bit 7 of `E813` gets cleared before the
2026-08-19 17:58:04 [gemini-3.7-flash] Kernal IRQ handler has a chance to inspect it.
