2026-08-19 18:05:14 [gemini-3.7-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.1 gemini-3.7-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.135 495.6KB 6.22s
2026-08-19 18:05:14 [gemini-3.7-flash] Understood: no full-file refactors, only targeted diffs and discussion.
2026-08-19 18:05:14 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 18:05:14 [gemini-3.7-flash] Here is the exact issue causing `INC $E810` to not cycle through the keyboard rows properly:
2026-08-19 18:05:14 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 18:05:14 [gemini-3.7-flash] The Cause
2026-08-19 18:05:14 [gemini-3.7-flash] In `readAddressBus()`, reads to `$E800` range are routed through `this.readPET(address)`. In your
2026-08-19 18:05:14 [gemini-3.7-flash] current code:
2026-08-19 18:05:14 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 18:05:14 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 18:05:14 [gemini-3.7-flash] case 0xe810: // PIA1_PA
2026-08-19 18:05:14 [gemini-3.7-flash] 	const cra = mem[0xE811];
2026-08-19 18:05:14 [gemini-3.7-flash] 	if ((cra&4)===0) {
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash] 		traceLog("[PET] read ddra",hex(this.ddra));
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash] 		return this.ddra;
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash] 	}
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash] 	mem[0xE811]&=0x3f;
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash] 	value=0xc0|(value&15);
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash] 	break;
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash] When `INC $E810` executes:
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash] 1. It reads `E810`, returning `0xC0 | (value & 15)` (e.g. `C0`).
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash] 2. It increments the value in the CPU (`C0` \rightarrow `C1`).
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash] 3. It writes `$C1` back via `writePET()`, which executes `scanKeyboard(value & 15)`.
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash] 4. However, inside `writePET(0xE810)`, the early `return` when `(cra & 4) === 0` is fine, but on
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash] normal writes `mem[address] = value` was being bypassed or masked out in `writeAddress`.
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash] The Diff
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash] Here is the simple diff for `readPET` and `writePET` to make sure the row select register stores
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash] and returns the latched row:
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash] --- a/machine.ts
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash] +++ b/machine.ts
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash] @@ -628,7 +628,7 @@ class Machine {
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash]  					return this.ddra;
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash]  				}
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash]  				mem[0xE811]&=0x3f;
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash] -				value=0xc0|(value&15);
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash] +				value=0xc0|(mem[0xE810]&15);
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash]  				break;
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash]  			case 0xe812: //	PIA1_PB
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash]  				const crb = mem[0xE813];
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash] @@ -669,6 +669,7 @@ class Machine {
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash]  		}
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash]  		const label=this.addresLabel(address);
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash]  		traceLog("[PET] write",label,hex(address),hex(value));
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash] +		mem[address]=value;
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash]  	}
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash] Discussion
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash] 1. `scanKeyboard(value & 15)` needs to tell your terminal/FFI matrix layer which row (0–9) is
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash] actively being driven low so that the subsequent `readPetMatrix()` call for `$E812` returns the 8
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash] column bits for that specific row.
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash] 2. In `readPetMatrix()`, unpressed keys must return `0xFF` (all bits high), and any pressed key
2026-08-19 18:05:15 [gemini-3.7-flash] must pull its column bit low (`0`).
