2026-08-19 18:37:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] The virtual-key codes for Left Shift and Right Shift depend on whether you are using the generic
2026-08-19 18:37:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] API code or side-specific codes:
2026-08-19 18:37:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 18:37:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] 1. Side-Specific Virtual Keys (Win32 / C++ API)
2026-08-19 18:37:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Left Shift (`VK_LSHIFT`): `160` (`0xA0`)
2026-08-19 18:37:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Right Shift (`VK_RSHIFT`): `161` (`0xA1`)
2026-08-19 18:37:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 18:37:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] 2. Standard / Generic Virtual Key (JavaScript `event.keyCode` / Win32 `VK_SHIFT`)
2026-08-19 18:37:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Left Shift: `16` (`0x10`)
2026-08-19 18:37:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Right Shift: `16` (`0x10`)
2026-08-19 18:37:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 18:37:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-08-19 18:37:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 18:37:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] In Modern JavaScript / TypeScript
2026-08-19 18:37:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] In browser environments, `event.keyCode` reports `16` for both. To differentiate between the two,
2026-08-19 18:37:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] check `event.code` or `event.location`:
2026-08-19 18:37:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 18:37:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Left Shift:
2026-08-19 18:37:52 [gemini-3.7-flash]   * `event.code === "ShiftLeft"`
2026-08-19 18:37:52 [gemini-3.7-flash]   * `event.location === 1` (`KeyboardEvent.DOM_KEY_LOCATION_LEFT`)
2026-08-19 18:37:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Right Shift:
2026-08-19 18:37:52 [gemini-3.7-flash]   * `event.code === "ShiftRight"`
2026-08-19 18:37:52 [gemini-3.7-flash]   * `event.location === 2` (`KeyboardEvent.DOM_KEY_LOCATION_RIGHT`)
2026-08-19 18:37:52 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
