2026-08-19 18:42:30 [nitro@ryzen5] what do emulators do for shifted numbers?
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.1 gemini-3.7-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.011 16.03KB 8.11s
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] Emulators generally take one of two approaches to handle shifted numbers and the differences
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] between modern PC layouts and the Commodore PET keyboard:
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] 1. Symbolic Mapping (Default / Recommended)
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] Because modern PC keyboards require `Shift` for `!` and output `1` unshifted, while the original
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] Commodore PET graphics keyboard did the exact opposite (unshifted gave symbols like `!`, shifted
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] gave digits like `1`), symbolic mapping translates the intended character into the correct
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] PET matrix combination.
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] In this mode, the emulator automatically modifies the PET shift state regardless of what the user
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] is physically pressing on the host keyboard:
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Host types `1` (Unshifted on PC):
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash]   * Emulator detects character `'1'`.
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash]   * PET matrix requires: Row 0, Col 0 + PET Shift Active.
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash]   * The emulator artificially activates the Shift bit in the matrix.
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Host types `Shift + 1` (`!` on PC):
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash]   * Emulator detects character `'!'`.
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash]   * PET matrix requires: Row 0, Col 0 + PET Shift Inactive.
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash]   * The emulator suppresses the host shift state and activates only the matrix bit.
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] Common Data Structure for Symbolic Mapping
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] Instead of storing just raw keycodes, symbolic mapping arrays or lookups often store a tuple or
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] bitmask indicating the target row, column, and forced shift behavior:
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] interface PetKeyMapping {
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] 	row: number;
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] 	col: number;
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] 	shiftState: "none" | "forceOn" | "forceOff" | "passThrough";
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] }
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] 2. Positional Mapping (Hardware Accurate)
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] Positional mapping binds the physical key position on a standard PC keyboard directly to the
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] equivalent electrical cross-point on the PET keyboard matrix:
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Host `Key1` always activates Row 0, Col 0.
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Host `LeftShift` always activates Row 8, Col 0.
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Effect:*
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Typing unshifted `1` on a PC will output `!` on a PET Graphics ROM.
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Typing `Shift + 1` on a PC will output `1` on a PET Graphics ROM.
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] This accurately simulates using the original physical hardware switches, but can be awkward for
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] users accustomed to standard typing layouts.
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] Summary of What Most Emulators (like VICE) Do
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] 1. Configurable Mode: They offer a toggle between Symbolic (translates characters
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] seamlessly) and Positional (1:1 physical switch emulation).
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] 2. Shift Inversion Logic: For the PET graphics keyboard specifically, symbolic mode inverts
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] the host's shift logic for the top numeric row.
2026-08-19 18:42:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] 3. Keypad Bypass: The numeric keypad on the PET graphics keyboard has dedicated number rows
2026-08-19 18:42:40 [gemini-3.7-flash] that do not require shift, so emulators often map PC numpad keys directly without shift alteration.
2026-08-19 18:42:40 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 18:44:21 [nitro@ryzen5] instead of backspace i am getting an inverse Q?
2026-08-19 18:44:41 [gemini-3.7-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.1 gemini-3.7-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.017 18.95KB 19.37s
2026-08-19 18:44:41 [gemini-3.7-flash] On Commodore PET systems, seeing an inverse `Q` when you press a key is almost always
2026-08-19 18:44:41 [gemini-3.7-flash] caused by one of two things:
2026-08-19 18:44:41 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 18:44:41 [gemini-3.7-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-08-19 18:44:41 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 18:44:41 [gemini-3.7-flash] 1. The PET is in "Quote Mode" or "Insert Mode"
2026-08-19 18:44:41 [gemini-3.7-flash] In PET BASIC / Kernal, control characters do not perform their normal action when the screen editor
2026-08-19 18:44:41 [gemini-3.7-flash] is in Quote Mode (after typing `"`) or Insert Mode (after pressing `Shift +
2026-08-19 18:44:41 [gemini-3.7-flash] INST/DEL`).
2026-08-19 18:44:41 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 18:44:41 [gemini-3.7-flash] Instead of moving the cursor or deleting, control codes print their reverse-video character
2026-08-19 18:44:41 [gemini-3.7-flash] representation:
2026-08-19 18:44:42 [gemini-3.7-flash] • `CRSR DOWN` / `CRSR UP` (PETSCII `11` / `91`) prints visually on screen as an
2026-08-19 18:44:42 [gemini-3.7-flash] inverted `Q`.
2026-08-19 18:44:42 [gemini-3.7-flash] • `INST / DEL` (PETSCII `14` / `94`) prints as an inverted `T`.
2026-08-19 18:44:42 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 18:44:42 [gemini-3.7-flash] If `Shift` is active when `INST/DEL` is triggered, the PET enters Insert Mode, causing
2026-08-19 18:44:42 [gemini-3.7-flash] subsequent cursor or control presses to display as inverted characters like inverse `Q`.
2026-08-19 18:44:42 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 18:44:42 [gemini-3.7-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-08-19 18:44:42 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 18:44:42 [gemini-3.7-flash] 2. Duplicate `8` in the Matrix Array
2026-08-19 18:44:42 [gemini-3.7-flash] In the matrix array above, `8` (the VK code for `Backspace / DEL`) was placed in two different
2026-08-19 18:44:42 [gemini-3.7-flash] positions:
2026-08-19 18:44:42 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Row 1, Col 6 (`INST/DEL`)
2026-08-19 18:44:42 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Row 8, Col 5
2026-08-19 18:44:42 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 18:44:42 [gemini-3.7-flash] If your lookup logic uses `petKeyCodes.indexOf(event.keyCode)` or loops linearly, duplicate numbers
2026-08-19 18:44:42 [gemini-3.7-flash] or misaligned columns will trigger the wrong matrix row/column (such as triggering the CRSR
2026-08-19 18:44:42 [gemini-3.7-flash] line instead of the INST/DEL line).
2026-08-19 18:44:42 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 18:44:42 [gemini-3.7-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-08-19 18:44:42 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 18:44:42 [gemini-3.7-flash] How to Fix
2026-08-19 18:44:42 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 18:44:42 [gemini-3.7-flash] 1. Clean up Row 8: Remove the duplicate `8` from Row 8 (col 5 on Row 8 is not INST/DEL).
2026-08-19 18:44:42 [gemini-3.7-flash] 2. Ensure Unshifted for Delete: Ensure that when the host sends `Backspace` (VK 8), your
2026-08-19 18:44:42 [gemini-3.7-flash] emulator clears the PET's `Shift` bit in the matrix. On real PET hardware:
2026-08-19 18:44:42 [gemini-3.7-flash]    * Unshifted `INST/DEL` = Delete (moves back and deletes character).
2026-08-19 18:44:42 [gemini-3.7-flash]    * Shifted `INST/DEL` = Insert space (and enters Insert mode).
2026-08-19 18:44:42 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
