2026-08-19 19:09:58 [nitro@ryzen5] is break key on pet a normal key, and does it stop basic
2026-08-19 19:10:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.1 gemini-3.7-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.010 27.45KB 4.91s
2026-08-19 19:10:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] Yes to both:
2026-08-19 19:10:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 19:10:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 1. Is it a normal key?
2026-08-19 19:10:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Yes. Unlike later machines such as the Commodore 64 or VIC-20 (which had a dedicated
2026-08-19 19:10:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] hardware `RESTORE` line wired directly to the CPU's Non-Maskable Interrupt), the
2026-08-19 19:10:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] `RUN/STOP`* key on the PET is simply a standard switch in the standard keyboard matrix
2026-08-19 19:10:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] (scanned via the 6520 PIA chip during the regular 60 Hz interrupt). It has no special electrical
2026-08-19 19:10:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] connection or dedicated hardware interrupt.
2026-08-19 19:10:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 19:10:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-08-19 19:10:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 19:10:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 2. Does it stop BASIC?
2026-08-19 19:10:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Yes.* While a BASIC program executes, the PET Kernal checks the keyboard matrix buffer.
2026-08-19 19:10:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] If it detects that `RUN/STOP` is pressed:
2026-08-19 19:10:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 19:10:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] • It immediately halts program execution.
2026-08-19 19:10:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] • It prints:
2026-08-19 19:10:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 19:10:03 [gemini-3.7-flash]   BREAK IN LINE <number>
2026-08-19 19:10:03 [gemini-3.7-flash]   READY.
2026-08-19 19:10:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 19:10:04 [gemini-3.7-flash] • You can resume execution from where it stopped by typing `CONT` and pressing `RETURN`.
2026-08-19 19:10:04 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 19:10:04 [gemini-3.7-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-08-19 19:10:04 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-19 19:10:04 [gemini-3.7-flash] Additional Behavior:
2026-08-19 19:10:04 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Unshifted: Acts as `STOP` (interrupts BASIC execution or stops screen
2026-08-19 19:10:04 [gemini-3.7-flash] listing/scrolling).
2026-08-19 19:10:04 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Shifted (`Shift + RUN/STOP`): Acts as `RUN` (initiates a tape `LOAD` and
2026-08-19 19:10:04 [gemini-3.7-flash] automatically issues `RUN` upon completion).
2026-08-19 19:10:04 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
