2026-08-20 09:32:16 [gemini-3.7-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.1 gemini-3.7-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.012 1.600KB 10.53s
2026-08-20 09:32:16 [gemini-3.7-flash] On the Commodore Plus/4, the `FD00–FDFF` page is allocated for I/O hardware registers
2026-08-20 09:32:16 [gemini-3.7-flash] (decoded by the PLA in 16-byte blocks).
2026-08-20 09:32:16 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-20 09:32:16 [gemini-3.7-flash] Here is how that region is mapped in stock hardware:
2026-08-20 09:32:16 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-20 09:32:16 [gemini-3.7-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-08-20 09:32:16 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-20 09:32:16 [gemini-3.7-flash] Stock Memory Map for `FD00–FD3F`
2026-08-20 09:32:16 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-20 09:32:16 [gemini-3.7-flash] • `FD00–FD0F`: MOS 6551 ACIA (RS-232 / Serial communication registers)
2026-08-20 09:32:16 [gemini-3.7-flash] • `FD10–FD1F`: MOS 6529B SPI (Single Port Interface for the 8-bit User Port)
2026-08-20 09:32:16 [gemini-3.7-flash] • `FD20–FD2F`: Unassigned / Open Bus
2026-08-20 09:32:16 [gemini-3.7-flash]   In the standard Plus/4 hardware, the PLA does not route `$FD20` to any internal motherboard chip.
2026-08-20 09:32:16 [gemini-3.7-flash] Reading from this address returns floating bus values (or ROM/RAM depending on memory
2026-08-20 09:32:16 [gemini-3.7-flash] configuration), and writing has no effect on stock internal hardware.
2026-08-20 09:32:16 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-20 09:32:16 [gemini-3.7-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-08-20 09:32:16 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-20 09:32:16 [gemini-3.7-flash] Common Nearby Registers Often Confused With `$FD20`
2026-08-20 09:32:16 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-20 09:32:16 [gemini-3.7-flash] If you are looking for a specific hardware function, it may be located at one of these related
2026-08-20 09:32:16 [gemini-3.7-flash] addresses:
2026-08-20 09:32:16 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-20 09:32:16 [gemini-3.7-flash] 1. User Port Data Register (`$FD10`)
2026-08-20 09:32:16 [gemini-3.7-flash]    Controls the 8-bit bidirectional User Port via the MOS 6529B.
2026-08-20 09:32:16 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-20 09:32:16 [gemini-3.7-flash] 2. Function ROM / "3+1" Bank Switching (`FDD0–FDDF`)
2026-08-20 09:32:16 [gemini-3.7-flash]    Reading or writing to this range selects internal/external ROM banks (used by the built-in
2026-08-20 09:32:16 [gemini-3.7-flash] software suite).
2026-08-20 09:32:16 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-20 09:32:16 [gemini-3.7-flash] 3. TED Chip Registers (`FF00–FF1F`)
2026-08-20 09:32:16 [gemini-3.7-flash]    The primary audio, video, timer, and interrupt registers of the MOS 7360/8360 (TED).
2026-08-20 09:32:16 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-20 09:32:16 [gemini-3.7-flash] 4. TED Register Mirrors (`FF20–FF3D`)
2026-08-20 09:32:16 [gemini-3.7-flash]    Addresses above `FF1F` mirror the main TED registers (e.g., `FF20` mirrors `$FF00`, the primary
2026-08-20 09:32:16 [gemini-3.7-flash] horizontal scroll / video mode control).
2026-08-20 09:32:16 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-20 09:32:16 [gemini-3.7-flash] 5. ROM / RAM Mode Switching (`FF3E` and `FF3F`)
2026-08-20 09:32:16 [gemini-3.7-flash]    Writing to `FF3E` enables the ROMs; writing to `FF3F` switches entirely to RAM.
