2026-08-20 09:32:55 [gemini-3.7-flash] Why this is in the Plus/4 ROM
2026-08-20 09:32:55 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-20 09:32:55 [gemini-3.7-flash] During development of the 264 series, Commodore developed several sibling models sharing a common
2026-08-20 09:32:55 [gemini-3.7-flash] architecture and KERNAL codebase:
2026-08-20 09:32:55 [gemini-3.7-flash] • C16 / C116 (Entry-level)
2026-08-20 09:32:55 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Plus/4 (Standard productivity model)
2026-08-20 09:32:55 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Commodore V364 (High-end prototype with built-in speech synthesis)
2026-08-20 09:32:55 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-20 09:32:55 [gemini-3.7-flash] The KERNAL code you are seeing at `$CFA6` is a remnant of the V364 speech initialization
2026-08-20 09:32:55 [gemini-3.7-flash] routine:
2026-08-20 09:32:55 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-20 09:32:55 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-20 09:32:55 [gemini-3.7-flash] CFA6: LDA #$09        ; Set control word for speech processor
2026-08-20 09:32:55 [gemini-3.7-flash] CFA8: STA $FD20       ; Write to speech chip register
2026-08-20 09:32:55 [gemini-3.7-flash] CFAB: ORA #$80        ; Set bit 7 (reset / strobe bit)
2026-08-20 09:32:55 [gemini-3.7-flash] CFAD: STA $FD20       ; Strobe the speech chip register
2026-08-20 09:32:55 [gemini-3.7-flash] CFB0: JMP $FC1E       ; Continue to Function ROM / cartridge scan ($FDD0)
2026-08-20 09:32:55 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-20 09:32:55 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
