2026-08-20 10:30:54 [gemini-3.7-flash] 1. The Banking Register Range (`FDD0–FDDF`)
2026-08-20 10:30:54 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-20 10:30:54 [gemini-3.7-flash] In the Plus/4 architecture, writing to (or reading from) addresses in the range `FDD0–FDDF`
2026-08-20 10:30:54 [gemini-3.7-flash] triggers hardware latches inside the PLA that switch the ROM banks mapped to the
2026-08-20 10:30:54 [gemini-3.7-flash] `8000–BFFF` (and in some configurations `C000–FFFF`) regions.
2026-08-20 10:30:54 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-20 10:30:54 [gemini-3.7-flash] The 16 addresses in `FDD0–FDDF` are decoded by their lowest 4 bits (`A0–A3`):
2026-08-20 10:30:54 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-20 10:30:54 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Bits 0–1 (`A0–A1`): Select the Bank Number (`0` to `3`)
2026-08-20 10:30:54 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Bits 2–3 (`A2–A3`): Select the ROM Socket / Location:
2026-08-20 10:30:54 [gemini-3.7-flash]   * `00` = BASIC / KERNAL (Standard system ROMs)
2026-08-20 10:30:54 [gemini-3.7-flash]   * `01` = Internal Function ROM High/Low (The built-in "3+1" software: Word Processor,
2026-08-20 10:30:54 [gemini-3.7-flash] Spreadsheet, etc.)
2026-08-20 10:30:54 [gemini-3.7-flash]   * `10` = External Cartridge ROM (Low / High) (Expansion port)
2026-08-20 10:30:54 [gemini-3.7-flash]   * `11` = Extended Function ROM / Cartridge Bank 3
2026-08-20 10:30:54 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
