2026-08-20 10:30:54 [gemini-3.7-flash] 3. Required Simulator Implementation
2026-08-20 10:30:54 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-20 10:30:54 [gemini-3.7-flash] To correctly handle this sequence in your memory controller:
2026-08-20 10:30:54 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-20 10:30:54 [gemini-3.7-flash] 1. Strobe Decoding on `FDD0–FDDF`:
2026-08-20 10:30:54 [gemini-3.7-flash]    * Intercept any read or write access to `FDD0–FDDF`.
2026-08-20 10:30:54 [gemini-3.7-flash]    * Extract the lower 4 bits `(address & 0x0F)`.
2026-08-20 10:30:54 [gemini-3.7-flash]    * Switch the active memory buffer mapped at `8000–BFFF` (and `C000–FFFF` if applicable) to match
2026-08-20 10:30:55 [gemini-3.7-flash] the selected internal ROM image, external cartridge file, or open bus/RAM if no ROM is plugged into
2026-08-20 10:30:55 [gemini-3.7-flash] that socket.
2026-08-20 10:30:55 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-20 10:30:55 [gemini-3.7-flash] 2. Open Bus Behavior for Empty Sockets:
2026-08-20 10:30:55 [gemini-3.7-flash]    * If an internal ROM (like the 3+1 suite) or cartridge is not loaded for a particular bank,
2026-08-20 10:30:55 [gemini-3.7-flash] reading `8007–8009` should not return `"CBM"`.
2026-08-20 10:30:55 [gemini-3.7-flash]    * In your current trace, all banks are returning `"CBM"`, which means the simulator is mapping
2026-08-20 10:30:55 [gemini-3.7-flash] the same ROM image across all banks or leaving data on the bus matching that signature.
