2026-08-20 10:52:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] 1. `$FD01 00` (MOS 6551 ACIA Reset)
2026-08-20 10:52:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Address `$FD01` is the Status / Programmed Reset Register of the MOS 6551 ACIA
2026-08-20 10:52:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] (the RS-232 serial chip).
2026-08-20 10:52:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Writing `$00` performs a software reset on the ACIA to clear its internal state, parity, and
2026-08-20 10:52:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] framing error flags.
2026-08-20 10:52:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-20 10:52:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-08-20 10:52:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-20 10:52:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] 2. `$FF08` Keyboard Matrix Reads
2026-08-20 10:52:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] • `$FF08` is the TED Keyboard Latch / Row register.
2026-08-20 10:52:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] • The KERNAL reads this register immediately after initializing hardware to check for special boot
2026-08-20 10:52:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] keys (such as the `STOP` or `C=` keys) to determine whether to abort normal startup or enter the
2026-08-20 10:52:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] machine code monitor.
2026-08-20 10:52:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Returning `7F` (or `FF` when no keys are pressed) indicates no boot-override keys are held down.
2026-08-20 10:52:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-20 10:52:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-08-20 10:52:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-20 10:52:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] 3. The `FFFD` \rightarrow `FFF6` Read / Write Sequence
2026-08-20 10:52:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] This sequence is the KERNAL copying the hardware vectors and Reset trampolines from ROM into
2026-08-20 10:52:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] the underlying RAM:
2026-08-20 10:52:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-20 10:52:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Why it does this:
2026-08-20 10:52:58 [gemini-3.7-flash]   When the Plus/4 switches out ROM to enable full 64KB RAM mode (via `FF3F`), the CPU still needs
2026-08-20 10:52:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] valid reset/interrupt vectors (`FFFA–FFFF`) and bank-switching code at `FFF6` in memory so an
2026-08-20 10:52:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] interrupt or switch back does not crash the system.
2026-08-20 10:52:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-20 10:52:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Memory Architecture Note:
2026-08-20 10:52:58 [gemini-3.7-flash]   In the Commodore architecture, when ROM is enabled:
2026-08-20 10:52:58 [gemini-3.7-flash]   * Reads from `FFF6–FFFF` fetch data from the KERNAL ROM.
2026-08-20 10:52:58 [gemini-3.7-flash]   * Writes to `FFF6–FFFF` pass directly through to the underlying RAM.
2026-08-20 10:52:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-20 10:52:58 [gemini-3.7-flash]   The loop reads the vector table from ROM (`LDA FFF6,X`) and writes it immediately back (`STA
2026-08-20 10:52:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] FFF6,X`), thereby copying the ROM vectors into the RAM underneath.
2026-08-20 10:52:58 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
