2026-08-20 10:55:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] Bit Breakdown
2026-08-20 10:55:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-20 10:55:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Page Filter (`address & 0xFD00 == 0xFD00`):
2026-08-20 10:55:39 [gemini-3.7-flash]   Isolates pages `%11111101` (`FD`) and `%11111111` (`FF`) in a single mask check.
2026-08-20 10:55:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Page Selector (`address & 0x0200`):
2026-08-20 10:55:39 [gemini-3.7-flash]   Checks bit 9 (`0` for `FDxx`, `1` for `FFxx`).
2026-08-20 10:55:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] • `FD00–FDDF` Decoding (`(address & 0x00E0) != 0x00E0`):
2026-08-20 10:55:39 [gemini-3.7-flash]   `FDE0–FDFF` has the top three bits (`%111x_xxxx`) set. Inverting this condition isolates `00–DF`.
2026-08-20 10:55:39 [gemini-3.7-flash] • `FF00–FF3F` Decoding (`(address & 0x00C0) == 0x0000`):
2026-08-20 10:55:39 [gemini-3.7-flash]   The lower 64 bytes (`00–3F`) have bits 7 and 6 cleared (`%00xx_xxxx`).
