2026-08-20 11:18:59 [gemini-3.7-flash] The Cause: Vector Copy Failure
2026-08-20 11:18:59 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-20 11:18:59 [gemini-3.7-flash] The writes to `FFF6–FFFD` are missing.
2026-08-20 11:18:59 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-20 11:18:59 [gemini-3.7-flash] The KERNAL executes this routine (`$F34E`):
2026-08-20 11:18:59 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-20 11:18:59 [gemini-3.7-flash] F34E: LDX #$07
2026-08-20 11:18:59 [gemini-3.7-flash] F350: LDA $FFF6,X   ; Read vector from ROM
2026-08-20 11:18:59 [gemini-3.7-flash] F353: STA $FFF6,X   ; Write vector to RAM
2026-08-20 11:18:59 [gemini-3.7-flash] F356: DEX
2026-08-20 11:18:59 [gemini-3.7-flash] F357: BPL $F350
2026-08-20 11:18:59 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-20 11:18:59 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-20 11:18:59 [gemini-3.7-flash] 1. Why these writes must succeed:
2026-08-20 11:18:59 [gemini-3.7-flash]    Immediately after this loop, the KERNAL performs the RAM sizing routine (`$F359`).
2026-08-20 11:18:59 [gemini-3.7-flash]    To test total available RAM, it writes `$FF3F` (switching the CPU to 100% all-RAM mode,
2026-08-20 11:18:59 [gemini-3.7-flash] disabling the KERNAL ROM).
2026-08-20 11:18:59 [gemini-3.7-flash]    It then executes code out of high memory and triggers routines via the reset/NMI vectors at
2026-08-20 11:18:59 [gemini-3.7-flash] `FFFA–FFFF`.
2026-08-20 11:18:59 [gemini-3.7-flash] 2. The Result:
2026-08-20 11:18:59 [gemini-3.7-flash]    If the writes to `FFF6–FFFF` were blocked, dropped, or treated as read-only ROM writes, then
2026-08-20 11:18:59 [gemini-3.7-flash] when `FF3F` switches to all-RAM mode, `FFF6–FFFF` contains uninitialized garbage (`00` or random
2026-08-20 11:18:59 [gemini-3.7-flash] data). The CPU jumps to `$0000` or an invalid address on the very next instruction or interrupt,
2026-08-20 11:18:59 [gemini-3.7-flash] causing a silent crash before the display screen is initialized or cleared.
2026-08-20 11:18:59 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
