2026-08-26 16:14:13 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] 
2026-08-26 16:14:13 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] How this handles your example
2026-08-26 16:14:13 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] 
2026-08-26 16:14:13 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] `👨‍👩‍👧‍👦` is a single grapheme cluster containing multiple code points joined by ZWJ. Our
2026-08-26 16:14:13 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] `graphemeWidth` detects the ZWJ and returns `2`. If your terminal renders the family as one
2026-08-26 16:14:13 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] glyph, this is correct. If it renders it as four separate emoji, the width should be
2026-08-26 16:14:13 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] `8`, and you’ll see jagged borders.
2026-08-26 16:14:13 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] 
2026-08-26 16:14:13 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] To cope with that, you can add a configuration switch:
2026-08-26 16:14:13 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] 
2026-08-26 16:14:13 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] 
2026-08-26 16:14:13 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] const EMOJI_SEQUENCE_WIDTH = 2; // set to 8 if your terminal renders ZWJ sequences as separate emoji
2026-08-26 16:14:13 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] 
2026-08-26 16:14:13 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] 
2026-08-26 16:14:13 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] Then use that constant in `graphemeWidth` instead of hard‑coding `2`.
2026-08-26 16:14:13 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] 
2026-08-26 16:14:13 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] Caveats to consider
2026-08-26 16:14:13 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] 
2026-08-26 16:14:13 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] - Ambiguous characters (box‑drawing, certain Greek, etc.) are treated as width 1. This
2026-08-26 16:14:13 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] matches Western terminals. If you’re targeting CJK terminals, you may want to treat them as 2.
2026-08-26 16:14:13 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] - Indentation – I’ve used tabs to match the rest of the file; adjust if your editor demands
2026-08-26 16:14:13 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] spaces.
2026-08-26 16:14:13 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] - Performance – `Intl.Segmenter` is efficient, but if you call `stringWidth` thousands of
2026-08-26 16:14:13 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] times per frame, consider caching results.
2026-08-26 16:14:13 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] 
2026-08-26 16:14:13 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] Now your desktop manager can draw boxes around mixed‑width text without breaking, as long as the
2026-08-26 16:14:13 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] terminal’s rendering matches the heuristic. If you find a terminal that defies the heuristic, let
2026-08-26 16:14:13 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] me know – you can quickly adapt the config flag.
