2026-08-26 16:49:49 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] Why this handles your 4‑head example well
2026-08-26 16:49:49 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] 
2026-08-26 16:49:49 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] With `Intl.Segmenter`, `👨‍👩‍👧‍👦` is returned as a single grapheme. Our `graphemeWidth` sees the
2026-08-26 16:49:49 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] ZWJ and returns `2`. If the terminal supports mode 2027, it will render as one wide glyph — so 2
2026-08-26 16:49:49 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] cells is correct. If it doesn’t, the terminal may render four separate emoji (8 cells), and your
2026-08-26 16:49:49 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] layout will be off. That’s the residual risk, which you can mitigate with the constant as
