2026-08-27 14:17:35 [glm-5.3-flash] Thanks for sharing — this is a neat little codebase. A few observations on things that stood out:
2026-08-27 14:17:35 [glm-5.3-flash] 
2026-08-27 14:17:35 [glm-5.3-flash] • Possible bugs*
2026-08-27 14:17:35 [glm-5.3-flash] 
2026-08-27 14:17:35 [glm-5.3-flash] - In `pollKeypad()`, Home and End look swapped: `case "[H"` sets `EndBit` and `case "[F"` sets
2026-08-27 14:17:35 [glm-5.3-flash] `HomeBit`. Most terminals send `[H` for Home and `[F` for End (matching the C1 codes
2026-08-27 14:17:35 [glm-5.3-flash] `[1;H`/`[1;F`). If this was deliberate for a specific terminal, worth a comment saying so.
2026-08-27 14:17:35 [glm-5.3-flash] - The `KeyBits` enum counts from zero (`UP=0, DOWN=1…`) so its members don't align with the
2026-08-27 14:17:35 [glm-5.3-flash] `UpBit=1, DownBit=2…` mask constants actually used below. The inline comments also repeat values
2026-08-27 14:17:35 [glm-5.3-flash] (`// 64 128` appears twice, and `SPACE,SHIFT` reuses the `// 16 32` pair). Since the enum isn't
2026-08-27 14:17:35 [glm-5.3-flash] referenced anywhere, it may be misleading rather than useful in its current form.
2026-08-27 14:17:35 [glm-5.3-flash] - SGR mouse parsing discards the `M`/`m` press/release terminator (it survives as text attached to
2026-08-27 14:17:35 [glm-5.3-flash] the last coordinate, harmlessly ignored by `parseInt`). As a workaround you XOR-toggle the button
2026-08-27 14:17:35 [glm-5.3-flash] bits, which roughly works — but `case 32` will fire on every motion event while a button is held
2026-08-27 14:17:35 [glm-5.3-flash] (SGR adds 32 for motion), so `MouseRightBit` will flicker rapidly during drags. Distinguishing
2026-08-27 14:17:35 [glm-5.3-flash] press from release needs that trailing character.
2026-08-27 14:17:35 [glm-5.3-flash] - `mouseButtons |= 4` for motion is never cleared, so the motion bit latches on permanently after
2026-08-27 14:17:35 [glm-5.3-flash] the first move.
2026-08-27 14:17:35 [glm-5.3-flash] - Escape sequences split across two stdin reads (common over SSH) will fail to parse. Buffering
2026-08-27 14:17:35 [glm-5.3-flash] partial reads until a complete sequence arrives would harden this.
2026-08-27 14:17:35 [glm-5.3-flash] 
2026-08-27 14:17:35 [glm-5.3-flash] • Smaller notes*
2026-08-27 14:17:35 [glm-5.3-flash] 
2026-08-27 14:17:35 [glm-5.3-flash] - `inputTask` is stored but never awaited, so a rejection in `runInputTask` could go unobserved.
2026-08-27 14:17:35 [glm-5.3-flash] - `class panel` with `rect: Uint16Array` and no initializer will trip
2026-08-27 14:17:35 [glm-5.3-flash] `strictPropertyInitialization` if you ever run `deno check`.
2026-08-27 14:17:35 [glm-5.3-flash] - `GRAPHEME_DISABLE` is sent at boot even though `terminal.ts` carries fairly careful
2026-08-27 14:17:35 [glm-5.3-flash] grapheme-width logic — I assume that's intentional because mode 2027 interferes with your manual
2026-08-27 14:17:35 [glm-5.3-flash] cell layout?
2026-08-27 14:17:35 [glm-5.3-flash] - Dead weight: `hex()`, `fadePumps()`'s return value, `oldKeys` change detection, and the
2026-08-27 14:17:35 [glm-5.3-flash] commented-out `gridHalfWindowLayer` call referencing functions that don't exist yet.
2026-08-27 14:17:35 [glm-5.3-flash] 
2026-08-27 14:17:35 [glm-5.3-flash] • On the README todo* — "basic mouse color grid" fits nicely with what's already plumbed:
2026-08-27 14:17:35 [glm-5.3-flash] `mousePosition` and the motion bit in `hitBits` give you everything needed to paint cells under the
2026-08-27 14:17:35 [glm-5.3-flash] cursor into a half-block grid, once `updateConsole` grows a real renderer.
2026-08-27 14:17:35 [glm-5.3-flash] 
2026-08-27 14:17:35 [glm-5.3-flash] Happy to dig into the platform-specific FFI/MIDI modules next, or sketch the color-grid renderer
2026-08-27 14:17:35 [glm-5.3-flash] whenever you're ready.
2026-08-27 14:17:35 [glm-5.3-flash] 
