2026-08-27 15:12:18 [glm-5.3-flash] hand-implementing F/W, treating H/Na/N as narrow, and leaving A (Ambiguous) unhandled, which
2026-08-27 15:12:18 [glm-5.3-flash] matches the docs' open question. An option flag for ambiguous-wide terminals could slot in later.
2026-08-27 15:12:18 [glm-5.3-flash] - Coverage gaps to be aware of: variation selectors (U+FE00–FE0F) aren't in the zero-width set, so
2026-08-27 15:12:18 [glm-5.3-flash] 🏳️ falls through to the `wideCount > 1` heuristic rather than explicit handling. Regional
