2026-08-27 15:28:55 [glm-5.3-flash] 
2026-08-27 15:28:55 [glm-5.3-flash] • time.ts*
2026-08-27 15:28:55 [glm-5.3-flash] - The frame width math mixes character counts with display cells. `timeString()` produces exactly
2026-08-27 15:28:55 [glm-5.3-flash] 32 characters (nice touch), but the fullwidth digits occupy 2 cells each, so the rendered line is
2026-08-27 15:28:55 [glm-5.3-flash] ~36 columns against a 32-column box — the right border will drift or overlap. Since you already
2026-08-27 15:28:55 [glm-5.3-flash] have `stringWidth()` in stringwidth.ts, padding the interior lines to a target cell width
2026-08-27 15:28:55 [glm-5.3-flash] via that function would make `frame()` safe for arbitrary content, including the todo's color grid
2026-08-27 15:28:56 [glm-5.3-flash] labels later.
