2026-08-27 15:28:56 [glm-5.3-flash] - Line 4 has a stray statement, `Intl.localesargument`, that looks like leftover scratch — it
2026-08-27 15:28:56 [glm-5.3-flash] evaluates to undefined so it won't throw, but it shouldn't ship.
2026-08-27 15:28:56 [glm-5.3-flash] - Flags like 🇺🇸 pass through your ranges by accident: regional indicators (U+1F1E6–1F1FF) sit
2026-08-27 15:28:56 [glm-5.3-flash] below your 0x1F300 emoji floor, so they score as narrow singles and sum to 2. Correct
2026-08-27 15:28:56 [glm-5.3-flash] answer, fragile reasoning — an explicit range or comment would prevent a future refactor from
2026-08-27 15:28:56 [glm-5.3-flash] breaking it.
2026-08-27 15:28:56 [glm-5.3-flash] - Coverage gaps versus EastAsianWidth: CJK Extensions B onward (U+20000+) are Wide and currently
2026-08-27 15:28:56 [glm-5.3-flash] width 1; U+3099–309A (combining katakana voicing marks) should be zero-width but land as 1. Your
2026-08-27 15:28:56 [glm-5.3-flash] blanket 2600–27BF generously covers most emoji-presentation symbols but also sweeps in some narrow
2026-08-27 15:28:56 [glm-5.3-flash] ones (scissors, ✔). Given the README's F/W/H/Na/N/A research, the "A" (Ambiguous) class is the one
