2026-08-28 22:16:24 [glm-5.3-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.2 glm-5.3-flash Z 🪠 0.7° $0.001 51.99KB 27.14s
2026-08-28 22:16:24 [glm-5.3-flash] In the Pico SDK, pin numbers are plain `uint` (unsigned int) — every function in `hardware/gpio.h`
2026-08-28 22:16:24 [glm-5.3-flash] takes it that way:
2026-08-28 22:16:24 [glm-5.3-flash] 
2026-08-28 22:16:24 [glm-5.3-flash] 
2026-08-28 22:16:24 [glm-5.3-flash] void gpio_init(uint gpio);
2026-08-28 22:16:24 [glm-5.3-flash] void gpio_set_dir(uint gpio, bool out);
2026-08-28 22:16:24 [glm-5.3-flash] void gpio_put(uint gpio, bool value);
2026-08-28 22:16:24 [glm-5.3-flash] 
2026-08-28 22:16:24 [glm-5.3-flash] 
2026-08-28 22:16:24 [glm-5.3-flash] So the declaration would be:
2026-08-28 22:16:24 [glm-5.3-flash] 
2026-08-28 22:16:24 [glm-5.3-flash] 
2026-08-28 22:16:24 [glm-5.3-flash] const uint gpio[]={0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7,14,15,16,17,18,19,20,21,22,26,27};
2026-08-28 22:16:24 [glm-5.3-flash] const uint gpioCount=sizeof(gpio)/sizeof(gpio[0]);
2026-08-28 22:16:24 [glm-5.3-flash] 
2026-08-28 22:16:24 [glm-5.3-flash] 
2026-08-28 22:16:24 [glm-5.3-flash] Two related types worth knowing:
2026-08-28 22:16:24 [glm-5.3-flash] 
2026-08-28 22:16:24 [glm-5.3-flash] - `gpio_dir_t` — in SDK 2.x, `gpio_set_dir` takes this enum (`GPIO_IN`, `GPIO_OUT`, `GPIO_IN_OUT`)
2026-08-28 22:16:24 [glm-5.3-flash] rather than a bool. In 1.x, `GPIO_IN`/`GPIO_OUT` were just `false`/`true`.
2026-08-28 22:16:24 [glm-5.3-flash] - `gpio_function` — the enum used by `gpio_set_function` (`GPIO_FUNC_SPI`, `GPIO_FUNC_PWM`,
2026-08-28 22:16:24 [glm-5.3-flash] `GPIO_FUNC_PIO0`, etc.).
2026-08-28 22:16:24 [glm-5.3-flash] 
2026-08-28 22:16:24 [glm-5.3-flash] `int` works fine in practice since pin numbers are small positives, but `uint` matches the SDK
2026-08-28 22:16:24 [glm-5.3-flash] signatures exactly and avoids sign-compare warnings in loops like `for(size_t
2026-08-28 22:16:24 [glm-5.3-flash] i=0;i<gpio.size();i++)`. If you keep the vector, `std::vector<uint>` would be the matching form —
2026-08-28 22:16:24 [glm-5.3-flash] though for a fixed pin list like this, the plain array is the more idiomatic SDK-style choice and
2026-08-28 22:16:24 [glm-5.3-flash] costs no heap.
2026-08-28 22:16:24 [glm-5.3-flash] 
