2026-08-28 22:46:59 [glm-5.3-flash] the `0xD0`/`0x90` differential commands) uses:
2026-08-28 22:46:59 [glm-5.3-flash] 
2026-08-28 22:46:59 [glm-5.3-flash] - TP_CS_PIN = 16 — chip select, driven low during reads
2026-08-28 22:46:59 [glm-5.3-flash] - TP_IRQ_PIN = 17 — interrupt, input with pull-up
2026-08-28 22:46:59 [glm-5.3-flash] 
2026-08-28 22:46:59 [glm-5.3-flash] The actual `#define`s live in picotool.h (this file just has them commented out as a reminder), so
2026-08-28 22:46:59 [glm-5.3-flash] verify there if the board has moved them.
2026-08-28 22:46:59 [glm-5.3-flash] 
2026-08-28 22:46:59 [glm-5.3-flash] The touch chip shares SPI_PORT with the LCD — `Touch_Read_ADC()` switches the baud rate
2026-08-28 22:46:59 [glm-5.3-flash] down to `TOUCH_SPI_BAUD` before a read and back up to `LCD_SPI_BAUD` after. The CLK/MOSI/MISO pins
2026-08-28 22:46:59 [glm-5.3-flash] themselves aren't touched by the touch code; the commented-out lines in `initTouch()` show the
2026-08-28 22:46:59 [glm-5.3-flash] `gpio_set_function` calls for `LCD_CLK_PIN`/`LCD_MOSI_PIN`/`LCD_MISO_PIN` were moved out, so touch
2026-08-28 22:46:59 [glm-5.3-flash] depends on the LCD init having already configured those pins for SPI.
2026-08-28 22:46:59 [glm-5.3-flash] 
2026-08-28 22:46:59 [glm-5.3-flash] Two current-state notes:
2026-08-28 22:46:59 [glm-5.3-flash] 
2026-08-28 22:46:59 [glm-5.3-flash] 1. `READ_TOUCH` is commented out at the top, so none of this compiles in at the moment —
2026-08-28 22:46:59 [glm-5.3-flash] `initTouch()` and `updateTouch()` are dead code as built.
2026-08-28 22:46:59 [glm-5.3-flash] 2. Pins 16 and 17 are in the `USE_ROM` GPIO vector, so if you re-enable touch while `USE_ROM` is
2026-08-28 22:46:59 [glm-5.3-flash] defined, the ROM input init will reset the CS/IRQ pins to plain SIO inputs after `initTouch()` has
2026-08-28 22:46:59 [glm-5.3-flash] configured them, depending on init order.
