2026-08-28 22:50:51 [glm-5.3-flash] The Waveshare 1.14" is an ST7789 panel, 240×135, 4-wire SPI. The standalone module has 8 signal
2026-08-28 22:50:51 [glm-5.3-flash] pins (on the 16-pin header, pins 9–16 are all just GND):
2026-08-28 22:50:51 [glm-5.3-flash] 
2026-08-28 22:50:51 [glm-5.3-flash] ╭──────────────┬──────────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────╮
2026-08-28 22:50:51 [glm-5.3-flash] │  Module pin  │  Function                        │  Maps to your code           │
2026-08-28 22:50:51 [glm-5.3-flash] ├──────────────┼──────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────┤
2026-08-28 22:50:51 [glm-5.3-flash] │  VCC         │  3.3V supply                     │  3V3                         │
2026-08-28 22:50:51 [glm-5.3-flash] │  GND         │  ground                          │  GND                         │
2026-08-28 22:50:51 [glm-5.3-flash] │  DIN         │  SPI MOSI                        │  `LCD_MOSI_PIN`              │
2026-08-28 22:50:51 [glm-5.3-flash] │  CLK         │  SPI SCK                         │  `LCD_CLK_PIN`               │
2026-08-28 22:50:51 [glm-5.3-flash] │  CS          │  LCD chip select, active low     │  `LCD_CS_PIN`                │
2026-08-28 22:50:51 [glm-5.3-flash] │  DC          │  data/command select             │  `LCD_DC_PIN`                │
2026-08-28 22:50:51 [glm-5.3-flash] │  RST         │  reset, active low               │  `LCD_RST_PIN`               │
2026-08-28 22:50:51 [glm-5.3-flash] │  BL          │  backlight, high = on, PWM-able  │  `LCD_BL_PIN` or tie to 3V3  │
2026-08-28 22:50:51 [glm-5.3-flash] ╰──────────────┴──────────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────╯
2026-08-28 22:50:51 [glm-5.3-flash] 
2026-08-28 22:50:51 [glm-5.3-flash] So four new GPIOs to allocate for CS/DC/RST/BL, and the bus keeps whatever MOSI/SCK your SPI_PORT
2026-08-28 22:50:51 [glm-5.3-flash] already uses.
2026-08-28 22:50:51 [glm-5.3-flash] 
2026-08-28 22:50:51 [glm-5.3-flash] Things that change versus your current panel:
2026-08-28 22:50:51 [glm-5.3-flash] 
2026-08-28 22:50:51 [glm-5.3-flash] - No MISO — the ST7789 is write-only. Any display readback has to go, and `readSPI()` loses
2026-08-28 22:50:51 [glm-5.3-flash] its only remaining user once touch is gone.
2026-08-28 22:50:51 [glm-5.3-flash] - No touch — the XPT2046 path stays out (it already is). TP_CS/TP_IRQ on 16/17 free up,
2026-08-28 22:50:51 [glm-5.3-flash] which also removes that collision with the `USE_ROM` vector we noted earlier.
2026-08-28 22:50:51 [glm-5.3-flash] - The 240×135 offset quirk — the ST7789's GRAM is 240×320, so landscape orientations need
2026-08-28 22:50:51 [glm-5.3-flash] column/row offsets (typically 52/40, varying with MADCTL rotation) or the image lands shifted and
2026-08-28 22:50:51 [glm-5.3-flash] wraps. That's driver-side, in wherever `CreatePicoDisplay()` gets its ST7789 init.
2026-08-28 22:50:51 [glm-5.3-flash] - Layout won't fit — the ROM pin indicator rects run to x=292 and the spiral reaches x=330,
2026-08-28 22:50:51 [glm-5.3-flash] both past 240. The time text at `LCD_HEIGHT-40` = 95 is fine vertically. Worth reworking those
2026-08-28 22:50:51 [glm-5.3-flash] coordinates while you're in there.
2026-08-28 22:50:51 [glm-5.3-flash] - Your palette code carries over — the byte-swapped RGB565 in `SetColor()` is exactly what
2026-08-28 22:50:51 [glm-5.3-flash] the ST7789 wants over SPI.
2026-08-28 22:50:52 [glm-5.3-flash] 
