2026-08-28 23:02:59 [glm-5.3-flash] `#ifdef` can't take operators — use `#if defined(...)` instead:
2026-08-28 23:02:59 [glm-5.3-flash] 
2026-08-28 23:02:59 [glm-5.3-flash] 
2026-08-28 23:02:59 [glm-5.3-flash] #if defined(WAVESHARE_TOUCHLCD_35) || defined(WAVESHARE_LCD_114)
2026-08-28 23:02:59 [glm-5.3-flash] 	// either board
2026-08-28 23:02:59 [glm-5.3-flash] #endif
2026-08-28 23:02:59 [glm-5.3-flash] 
2026-08-28 23:02:59 [glm-5.3-flash] 
2026-08-28 23:02:59 [glm-5.3-flash] Variants worth knowing:
2026-08-28 23:02:59 [glm-5.3-flash] 
2026-08-28 23:02:59 [glm-5.3-flash] 
2026-08-28 23:02:59 [glm-5.3-flash] #if defined(A) && defined(B)	// both
2026-08-28 23:02:59 [glm-5.3-flash] #if defined(A) && !defined(B)	// A but not B
2026-08-28 23:02:59 [glm-5.3-flash] #if !defined(A) && !defined(B)	// neither
2026-08-28 23:02:59 [glm-5.3-flash] 
2026-08-28 23:02:59 [glm-5.3-flash] 
2026-08-28 23:02:59 [glm-5.3-flash] Note it's `defined(X)`, not `defined(X)` with parentheses around the whole thing, and the macros
2026-08-28 23:03:00 [glm-5.3-flash] don't need to have a value — `#define WAVESHARE_LCD_114` alone is enough for `defined()` to be
2026-08-28 23:03:00 [glm-5.3-flash] true.
2026-08-28 23:03:00 [glm-5.3-flash] 
2026-08-28 23:03:00 [glm-5.3-flash] For your case, a pattern that works well with two boards sharing one driver:
2026-08-28 23:03:00 [glm-5.3-flash] 
2026-08-28 23:03:00 [glm-5.3-flash] 
2026-08-28 23:03:00 [glm-5.3-flash] #if defined(WAVESHARE_TOUCHLCD_35)
2026-08-28 23:03:00 [glm-5.3-flash] 	#define LCD_WIDTH	320
2026-08-28 23:03:00 [glm-5.3-flash] 	#define LCD_HEIGHT	240
2026-08-28 23:03:00 [glm-5.3-flash] 	#define READ_TOUCH
2026-08-28 23:03:00 [glm-5.3-flash] #elif defined(WAVESHARE_LCD_114)
2026-08-28 23:03:00 [glm-5.3-flash] 	#define LCD_WIDTH	240
2026-08-28 23:03:00 [glm-5.3-flash] 	#define LCD_HEIGHT	135
2026-08-28 23:03:00 [glm-5.3-flash] #endif
2026-08-28 23:03:00 [glm-5.3-flash] 
2026-08-28 23:03:00 [glm-5.3-flash] 
2026-08-28 23:03:00 [glm-5.3-flash] That way the rest of the code tests one macro at a time, and the board selection happens in one
2026-08-28 23:03:00 [glm-5.3-flash] place — ideally in CMake (`target_compile_definitions(... WAVESHARE_LCD_114=1)`) rather than edited
2026-08-28 23:03:00 [glm-5.3-flash] in the source, so switching boards is a build-config change.
