2026-08-28 23:08:14 [glm-5.3-flash] in the file length is the removed `//`). That's worth flagging first, because it cuts across the
2026-08-28 23:08:14 [glm-5.3-flash] 1.14 downgrade:
2026-08-28 23:08:14 [glm-5.3-flash] 
2026-08-28 23:08:14 [glm-5.3-flash] - The 1.14 has no touch controller, so there's nothing on the end of the reads.
2026-08-28 23:08:14 [glm-5.3-flash] - TP_CS/TP_IRQ (GP16/17) sit inside the `USE_ROM` vector, and `initTouch()` runs before the
2026-08-28 23:08:14 [glm-5.3-flash] ROM init loop in `picoInstance()` — so the ROM loop resets CS back to a plain input and touch is
2026-08-28 23:08:14 [glm-5.3-flash] dead even if a chip were attached.
