2026-08-29 12:11:46 [gemini-3.7-flash] Here is the updated script that constructs and attaches a large cube mesh dynamically in code:
2026-08-29 12:11:46 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-29 12:11:46 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-29 12:11:46 [gemini-3.7-flash] extends Node3D
2026-08-29 12:11:46 [gemini-3.7-flash] ## Continuous rotation with a dynamic cube mesh
2026-08-29 12:11:46 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-29 12:11:46 [gemini-3.7-flash] @export var speed_y: float = 1.5
2026-08-29 12:11:46 [gemini-3.7-flash] @export var speed_x: float = 0.5
2026-08-29 12:11:46 [gemini-3.7-flash] @export var cube_size: Vector3 = Vector3(10.0, 10.0, 10.0)
2026-08-29 12:11:46 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-29 12:11:46 [gemini-3.7-flash] var mesh_instance: MeshInstance3D
2026-08-29 12:11:46 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-29 12:11:47 [gemini-3.7-flash] func _ready() -> void:
2026-08-29 12:11:47 [gemini-3.7-flash] 	setup_cube_mesh()
2026-08-29 12:11:47 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-29 12:11:47 [gemini-3.7-flash] func _process(delta: float) -> void:
2026-08-29 12:11:47 [gemini-3.7-flash] 	rotate_y(speed_y * delta)
2026-08-29 12:11:47 [gemini-3.7-flash] 	rotate_x(speed_x * delta)
2026-08-29 12:11:47 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-29 12:11:47 [gemini-3.7-flash] func setup_cube_mesh() -> void:
2026-08-29 12:11:47 [gemini-3.7-flash] 	var box_mesh: BoxMesh = BoxMesh.new()
2026-08-29 12:11:47 [gemini-3.7-flash] 	box_mesh.size = cube_size
2026-08-29 12:11:47 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-29 12:11:47 [gemini-3.7-flash] 	mesh_instance = MeshInstance3D.new()
2026-08-29 12:11:47 [gemini-3.7-flash] 	mesh_instance.mesh = box_mesh
2026-08-29 12:11:47 [gemini-3.7-flash] 	add_child(mesh_instance)
2026-08-29 12:11:47 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-29 12:11:47 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-29 12:11:47 [gemini-3.7-flash] You can adjust `cube_size` directly in the Inspector to scale the dimensions as needed.
2026-08-29 12:11:47 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
