2026-08-29 12:13:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] There are three common reasons this happens:
2026-08-29 12:13:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-29 12:13:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] 1. The `TextEdit` UI is covering the viewport:
2026-08-29 12:13:57 [gemini-3.7-flash]    If the networking script and the 3D node are running in the same scene, the `log_view`
2026-08-29 12:13:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] `TextEdit` control is sized to `1152×648` (default window dimensions). Because UI control nodes
2026-08-29 12:13:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] render on top of 3D viewports by default and `TextEdit` is opaque, it completely hides whatever is
2026-08-29 12:13:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] rendering behind it.
2026-08-29 12:13:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-29 12:13:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] 2. Missing or poorly positioned `Camera3D`:
2026-08-29 12:13:57 [gemini-3.7-flash]    3D geometry requires an active `Camera3D` in the scene to be drawn. Furthermore, because the
2026-08-29 12:13:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] cube is 10×10×10 units at the origin `(0, 0, 0)`, a camera placed at default coordinates `(0, 0,
2026-08-29 12:13:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] 0)` will sit inside the cube. A camera positioned back along the Z-axis (for example, at `(0, 5,
2026-08-29 12:13:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] 20)`) and pointed toward `(0, 0, 0)` is required to view it.
2026-08-29 12:13:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-29 12:13:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] 3. Active scene tab selection:
2026-08-29 12:13:57 [gemini-3.7-flash]    Pressing F6 runs whichever scene tab is currently open and focused in the editor. If the
2026-08-29 12:13:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] networking scene tab is active rather than the 3D cube scene, Godot will execute the network
2026-08-29 12:13:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] diagnostics scene instead.
2026-08-29 12:13:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-29 12:13:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] If you would like, I can provide the GDScript to dynamically create and position a `Camera3D` and a
2026-08-29 12:13:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] `DirectionalLight3D` automatically within the script.
2026-08-29 12:13:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
