2026-08-29 12:19:36 [gemini-3.7-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.2 gemini-3.7-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.003 15.72KB 5.11s
2026-08-29 12:19:36 [gemini-3.7-flash] To move the camera outside the cube, you can adjust either the position of the camera or the
2026-08-29 12:19:36 [gemini-3.7-flash] position of the `Node3D` cube.
2026-08-29 12:19:36 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-29 12:19:36 [gemini-3.7-flash] Method 1: Adjusting via the Editor Inspector
2026-08-29 12:19:36 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Move the Camera (Recommended):
2026-08-29 12:19:36 [gemini-3.7-flash]   1. Select your `Camera3D` node in the Scene dock.
2026-08-29 12:19:36 [gemini-3.7-flash]   2. In the Inspector panel on the right, look under the Transform section.
2026-08-29 12:19:36 [gemini-3.7-flash]   3. Change the Position Z coordinate to around `20.0` or `25.0` (since your cube extends 5
2026-08-29 12:19:36 [gemini-3.7-flash] units in each direction from the origin).
2026-08-29 12:19:36 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Move the Cube:
2026-08-29 12:19:36 [gemini-3.7-flash]   1. Select the `Node3D` containing the spinning cube script.
2026-08-29 12:19:36 [gemini-3.7-flash]   2. In the Inspector under Transform, change the Position Z coordinate to `-20.0`
2026-08-29 12:19:36 [gemini-3.7-flash] (pushing it into the distance away from the camera).
2026-08-29 12:19:36 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-29 12:19:36 [gemini-3.7-flash] Method 2: Adjusting in the 3D Viewport
2026-08-29 12:19:36 [gemini-3.7-flash] 1. Select the node in the Scene dock.
2026-08-29 12:19:36 [gemini-3.7-flash] 2. Ensure the Move tool is active (press `W`).
2026-08-29 12:19:36 [gemini-3.7-flash] 3. Click and drag the blue arrow (Z-axis) to reposition it in the scene until the cube is
2026-08-29 12:19:36 [gemini-3.7-flash] clearly visible.
2026-08-29 12:19:36 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-29 12:19:36 [gemini-3.7-flash] If you would like the script to handle positioning the camera and adding directional lighting
2026-08-29 12:19:36 [gemini-3.7-flash] automatically via code, please let me know.
