2026-08-29 12:21:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] A few important details regarding this combined snippet:
2026-08-29 12:21:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-29 12:21:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] 1. File Separation
2026-08-29 12:21:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] In GDScript, each script file can only have a single `extends` statement at the top. The network
2026-08-29 12:21:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] diagnostics logic (`extends Node`) and the 3D spinning cube logic (`extends Node3D`) must reside in
2026-08-29 12:21:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] separate `.gd` files attached to their respective nodes in the scene tree.
2026-08-29 12:21:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-29 12:21:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-08-29 12:21:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-29 12:21:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] 2. Positioning via Code (`transform3D`)
2026-08-29 12:21:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] In Godot 4, the commented `# transform3D(0,0,1)` line can be achieved directly using the `position`
2026-08-29 12:21:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] property:
2026-08-29 12:21:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-29 12:21:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Local Position: `position = Vector3(0.0, 0.0, -20.0)`
2026-08-29 12:21:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Global Position: `global_position = Vector3(0.0, 0.0, -20.0)`
2026-08-29 12:21:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-29 12:21:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] Setting the Z coordinate to a negative value (e.g., `-20.0`) pushes the cube 20 units in front of a
2026-08-29 12:21:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] default camera located at `(0, 0, 0)`.
2026-08-29 12:21:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-29 12:21:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-08-29 12:21:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-29 12:21:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] Please let me know if you would like me to provide the updated script with positioning or camera
2026-08-29 12:21:57 [gemini-3.7-flash] setup included.
