2026-08-29 12:24:13 [gemini-3.7-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.2 gemini-3.7-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° (undefined+NaN[13142]) 23.82KB 2.43s
2026-08-29 12:24:13 [gemini-3.7-flash] Yes, Godot handles fullscreen shortcuts differently depending on whether you are in the
2026-08-29 12:24:13 [gemini-3.7-flash] Editor or running the Game Window:
2026-08-29 12:24:13 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-29 12:24:13 [gemini-3.7-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-08-29 12:24:13 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-29 12:24:13 [gemini-3.7-flash] 1. In the Godot Editor
2026-08-29 12:24:13 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Shift + F11 (Windows/Linux) or Shift + Cmd + F (macOS): Toggles fullscreen mode
2026-08-29 12:24:13 [gemini-3.7-flash] for the entire Godot Editor.
2026-08-29 12:24:14 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Ctrl + Shift + F11 (Windows/Linux) or Ctrl + Cmd + F (macOS): Toggles fullscreen
2026-08-29 12:24:14 [gemini-3.7-flash] for the active editor viewport or workspace tab (3D/2D/Script view).
2026-08-29 12:24:14 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-29 12:24:14 [gemini-3.7-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-08-29 12:24:14 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-29 12:24:14 [gemini-3.7-flash] 2. In the Running Game Window
2026-08-29 12:24:14 [gemini-3.7-flash] By default, the running debug instance does not bind a built-in shortcut to toggle fullscreen, but
2026-08-29 12:24:14 [gemini-3.7-flash] you can configure one in two standard ways:
2026-08-29 12:24:14 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-29 12:24:14 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Always start in fullscreen:
2026-08-29 12:24:14 [gemini-3.7-flash]   Go to Project → Project Settings → Display → Window → Mode and set it to `fullscreen` (or
2026-08-29 12:24:14 [gemini-3.7-flash] `exclusive_fullscreen`).
2026-08-29 12:24:14 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-29 12:24:14 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Toggle fullscreen at runtime via GDScript:
