2026-08-29 17:12:26 [nitro@ryzen5] in gd what is console.log
2026-08-29 17:12:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.2 gemini-3.7-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.002 9.505KB 4.70s
2026-08-29 17:12:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] In GDScript, the equivalent of `console.log()` is the built-in function `print()`.
2026-08-29 17:12:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-29 17:12:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] There are also a few related logging functions available depending on the use case:
2026-08-29 17:12:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-29 17:12:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] • `print(...)` — Prints the provided arguments to the Godot Output panel and standard
2026-08-29 17:12:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] output, separated by spaces.
2026-08-29 17:12:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] • `print_debug(...)` — Similar to `print()`, but also appends the current file name, line
2026-08-29 17:12:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] number, and stack frame when running in debug mode.
2026-08-29 17:12:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] • `print_rich(...)` — Allows BBCode formatting (such as colors and bold text) within the
2026-08-29 17:12:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] Godot editor console.
2026-08-29 17:12:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] • `printerr(...)` — The equivalent of `console.error()`, directing output to standard error
2026-08-29 17:12:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] and formatting it in red within the editor console.
2026-08-29 17:12:31 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
