2026-08-29 17:32:28 [gemini-3.7-flash] In Godot's `WebSocketPeer`, the constant for the open state is:
2026-08-29 17:32:28 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-29 17:32:28 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-29 17:32:28 [gemini-3.7-flash] WebSocketPeer.STATE_OPEN
2026-08-29 17:32:28 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-29 17:32:28 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-29 17:32:28 [gemini-3.7-flash] Its underlying integer value is `1`.
2026-08-29 17:32:28 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-29 17:32:28 [gemini-3.7-flash] To check if a specific peer connection is open, compare the result of `get_ready_state()` with that
2026-08-29 17:32:28 [gemini-3.7-flash] constant:
2026-08-29 17:32:28 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-29 17:32:28 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-29 17:32:28 [gemini-3.7-flash] if peer.get_ready_state() == WebSocketPeer.STATE_OPEN:
2026-08-29 17:32:28 [gemini-3.7-flash] 	# Connection is established and ready for data
2026-08-29 17:32:28 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-29 17:32:28 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-29 17:32:28 [gemini-3.7-flash] For reference, the complete enum values under `WebSocketPeer.State` are:
2026-08-29 17:32:28 [gemini-3.7-flash] • `WebSocketPeer.STATE_CONNECTING` (0)
2026-08-29 17:32:28 [gemini-3.7-flash] • `WebSocketPeer.STATE_OPEN` (1)
2026-08-29 17:32:28 [gemini-3.7-flash] • `WebSocketPeer.STATE_CLOSING` (2)
2026-08-29 17:32:28 [gemini-3.7-flash] • `WebSocketPeer.STATE_CLOSED` (3)
