2026-08-30 19:27:53 [gemini-3.7-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.2 gemini-3.7-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.002 1.141KB 3.54s
2026-08-30 19:27:53 [gemini-3.7-flash] The standard way to convert an integer to a string in modern C++ is by using the `std::to_string`
2026-08-30 19:27:53 [gemini-3.7-flash] function, which is available in the `<string>` header.
2026-08-30 19:27:53 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-30 19:27:53 [gemini-3.7-flash] Other standard alternatives include:
2026-08-30 19:27:53 [gemini-3.7-flash] • `std::format` (available since C++20 in the `<format>` header)
2026-08-30 19:27:53 [gemini-3.7-flash] • `std::to_chars` (available since C++17 in the `<charconv>` header for high-performance
2026-08-30 19:27:53 [gemini-3.7-flash] conversions)
2026-08-30 19:27:53 [gemini-3.7-flash] • `std::stringstream` (in the `<sstream>` header)
2026-08-30 19:27:53 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-30 19:27:53 [gemini-3.7-flash] Please let me know if you would like code examples demonstrating any of these approaches.
